━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Markup is facet of Checker
    sees Assignments
    sees CallTyping
    sees Comprehensions
    sees LiveActions
    sees Styles

────────────────────
+ do leave-region

` Keeps what the assignments of the body of a `do without gc` block left each local it captures as,
` for the function around it to take once the body is checked (`check-region`): that holds after
` the block as after a plain one.
for row in frame.assigned-in-frame
    if !is-member-key(row.key) && frame.is-captured(row.key)
        region-left += row

────────────────────
+ do clashes-element Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - content SyntaxId

if content == 0 || no-receiver || types.intrinsic-of(receiver) != .class
    = false
.. no-receiver = receiver == no-type || receiver == invalid-type
. root = tree.root-this(content)
for node in tree.subtree-start(content) .. < content
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-markup(row)
            if named-element && clashes-property(receiver, node, row.id, row.type-id)
                = true
            .. named-element = row.id != 0 && node != root && !tree.enclosed-element(node, content)
= false

────────────────────
_ do clashes-property Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId

. text = tree.identifier-name(name)
. place = property-named(receiver, text) if text
if !place || names-element(types, types.properties[place])
    = false
. property = types.properties[place]
. held = property.type
if held == no-type
    held = demand-member(property, receiver, text!)
types.clear-fault()
. made = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, written, frame.env)
types.clear-fault()
if held == no-type || held == invalid-type || made == invalid-type || generic
    = false
.. generic = types.completions[made].has-variables
if holds-object(made, held)
    = false
. message = "Named markup element \"${text!.text}\" clashes with property \"${text!.text}\", which holds ${type-source(types, held)}, not ${type-source(types, made)}; rename the element"
frame.diagnose(element, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
= true

────────────────────
_ holds-object Bool
    - made TypeId
    - held TypeId

|? kind == .relation-side-cast && types.is-optional(held)
    holds-object(made, types.optional-inner(held))
??
    direct || interface-cast || kind == .relation-or-cast || kind == .relation-wrap-cast

.. kind = relations.compare(made, held).kind
.. direct = kind == .relation-same || kind == .relation-equal || kind == .relation-up-cast
.. interface-cast = kind == .relation-interface-cast

────────────────────
+ do waits-for-markup Bool
    - level TypeId
    - module ModuleId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` Whether a rule a class writes runs once the markup of the class has, as the reference runs
` it, rather than once a constructor's body has: where the class, or one above it, writes
` markup, each section that subscribes to a stream does, and so does a `when` or `whenever`
` rule whose test reads a member of a name the markup gives an element, apart from the
` functions written there.
if !writes-content(level)
    = false
. tree = program.modules[module].tree
. test SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[syntax]
    | .node-subscriber-syntax
        = true
    | .node-when-rule-syntax(rule)
        test = rule.expr
    | .node-whenever-rule-syntax(rule)
        test = rule.expr
if test == 0
    = false
. floor = tree.subtree-start(test)
. node = test + 1
while node > floor
    node -= 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-function-syntax
            node = tree.subtree-start(node)
        | .node-get-expression(get)
            do match? tree.nodes[get.object]
                | .node-identifier(read)
                    . place = property-named(level, read.name)
                    if place && names-element(types, types.properties[place])
                        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do own-markup-actions
    - receiver TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` How the function being typed makes the live actions the object it makes or fills owns, where
` its class is a markup host or batch, as the reference's `createMarkupAction` makes them with
` the object as owner: for a markup host, the markup runtime's `make-owner-markup-action`,
` given the object as its host, else `make-markup-action`, given it as the batch, each
` converted at `site`. It is noted only where a value or rule it runs is live
` (`live-owned`), and otherwise noted with none, so that a plain action is made for no such
` object. Either may raise.
if receiver == no-type || receiver == invalid-type || owns-plain-actions(receiver)
    =
if !live-owned
    facts.self-actions += SelfAction(instance, site, no-instance, false)
    =
. host = derived-interface(receiver, types.markup-host-decl)
. rooted = host == no-type
. wanted = if rooted then batch-type() else host
demand-live-runtime()
. live = instances.live
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push
    - if live.trackers != no-instance then instances.signatures[live.trackers].returns else no-type
scratch.types.push(live.callback)
scratch.types.push(wanted)
. action = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.markup-host-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom(if rooted then "make-markup-action" else "make-owner-markup-action")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if action == no-instance || live.has-actions == no-instance || wrong-return
    decline(site)
    =
.. wrong-return = instances.signatures[action].returns != types.live-action-type
if !raises-out(site, action)
    decline(site)
    =
if rooted
    conversions.convert(site, site, receiver, wanted, .reason-markup-batch)
else
    do host-self(receiver, site)
facts.self-actions += SelfAction(instance, site, action, rooted)

────────────────────
+ do is-ancestor-query Bool
    - query TypeId

` Whether a query of the markup an object is in looks for an ancestor, `Ancestor'T`.
do match? types.rows[query]
    | .type-class(row)
        = types.ancestor-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
= false

────────────────────
+ do trigger-target TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - syntax SyntaxId

` The class a rule a class or a facet of one writes looks for among the children or descendants
` of the object's markup host, `whenever children T` or `whenever descendants T`, where it is a
` markup host, or no type.
. env = holder-env(ref)
. type = rule-target(ref.module, syntax, env)
types.env-release(env)
= type

────────────────────
+ do markup-query U32
    - level TypeId
    - query TypeId
    - site SyntaxId
    - written-module ModuleId
    - written SyntaxId
    - name Atom?

` The row of `markup-queries` for a property a class declares as a query of the markup its
` object is in, recorded the first time a constructor registers it, and found by the class and
` the property after that, taking again where the property is written, which an edit typed again
` in place may move (`retype-edit`): the functions the reference makes for it read the object as
` one of the class, made its markup host as converted here, and call the markup runtime to find
` a parent host, or to add an object to a list kept in order or take one from it. The class and
` the class the query looks for must be markup hosts, which the reference reports, and the latter
` must declare no `==`, since a new answer is compared with the old as one object. Those have no
` shape here.
. place = property-named(level, name) if name
if !place
    decline(site)
    = U32.max
for offset in 0 .. < facts.markup-queries.length
    if same-level && facts.markup-queries[offset].place == place as U32
        facts.markup-queries[offset].module = written-module
        facts.markup-queries[offset].site = written
        = offset as U32
    .. same-level = facts.markup-queries[offset].level == level
. target = query-target(query)
. ancestor = is-ancestor-query(query)
if !is-markup-host(level) || !is-markup-host(target)
    decline(site)
    = U32.max
for token in ["==", "!="]
    if calls.has-operator(target, program.store-atom(token), target)
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
. host = derived-interface(level, types.markup-host-decl)
. held = types.properties[place].type
. module = types.markup-host-decl.module
. row = MarkupQuery
    - level
    - place as U32
    - written-module
    - written
    - target
    - 0
    - no-fact
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
. mark = scratch.types.mark
if ancestor
    scratch.types.push(host)
    row.parent = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - module
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("markup-query-parent-host")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if row.parent == no-instance || held != types.optional-of(target)
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
else
    . found = facts.query-targets.find(target)
    if !found
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
    row.target-id = (found + 1) as U32
    scratch.types.push(held)
    scratch.types.push(host)
    scratch.types.push(target)
    row.add = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - module
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("markup-query-add-descendant")
        - mark
    row.remove = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - module
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("markup-query-remove-descendant")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if row.add == no-instance || row.remove == no-instance
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
. recorded = facts.conversions.length
conversions.convert(0, 0, level, host, .reason-markup-host)
if unrecorded || facts.conversions[recorded].from != level || facts.conversions[recorded].to != host
    decline(site)
    = U32.max
.. unrecorded = facts.conversions.length == recorded
row.hosted = recorded as FactId
facts.markup-queries += row
= (facts.markup-queries.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
_ do element-context U32
    - class TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` The styles and style sheets a markup element of a class sees, which the reference hands the
` constructor of a class whose markup is its content, to make it under them
` (`markupStyleContextFor`): the element's vocabulary (`style-vocabulary`), the sheets it sees
` (`visible-sheets`) and the rules written in rules it sees, with those its own rules bring into
` view (`push-scopes`), as a context among `instances.contexts`; the sheets alone for a class
` that writes none but whose defaults apply rules (`defaults-apply-rules`); none for any other
` class, or where there are none. Each rule written in a rule under the state cell of a `when`
` gives the constructor the cell (`CarriedCell`), in turn, and then the values of each rule
` around rules written in it that takes some, once each (`CarriedValues`). `U32.max - 1` where
` it is declined: where they are not known here, or a using is.
if types.intrinsic-of(class) != .class || !program.module-by-name("core/style")
    = U32.max
. content = writes-content(class)
if !content && !defaults-apply-rules(class)
    = U32.max
if !sheets-known()
    decline(id)
    = U32.max - 1
. styles [TypeId]
if content
    . seen = style-vocabulary(class, id)
    if !seen
        = U32.max - 1
    styles = seen
. sheets [TypeId]
. levels [U32]
if types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo") != invalid-type
    visible-sheets(class, sheets, levels)
if !content && sheets.length == 0
    = U32.max
. scopes [RuleScope]
. cells [U32]
. carried [U32]
. valued [U32]
. value-types [TypeId]
. rows [U32]
if content
    if !scopes-known() && nested-any()
        decline(id)
        = U32.max - 1
    . seen = rule-scopes.length
    push-scopes(id)
    . next U32
    for use in rule-scopes
        scopes += use.scope
        . count = use-cells(use)
        cells += count
        if count != 0
            facts.link-cells(use.outer-cells, carried)
            carried += use.cell
            next += count
    . known = place-values(next, valued, value-types, rows)
    while rule-scopes.length > seen
        rule-scopes.pop()
    if !known
        decline(id)
        = U32.max - 1
. recorded = false
for held in facts.carried-cells
    recorded = recorded || (held.instance == instance && held.site == id)
for held in facts.carried-values
    recorded = recorded || (held.instance == instance && held.site == id)
if !recorded
    for cell in carried
        facts.carried-cells += CarriedCell(instance, id, cell)
    for row in rows
        facts.carried-values += CarriedValues(instance, id, row)
= instances.intern-context(styles, sheets, levels, scopes, cells, no-type, 0, valued, value-types)

────────────────────
+ do content-context U32

` The context the function that fills an object with its class's markup is made under, as
` `load-context` took it, which it hands the function of the class above: with the rules
` written in rules of the markup that made the object as it was given them, but not those its own
` markup brings into view, with the state cells it was given, which it gives on; and where a rule
` `• This` holds rules (`scoping-names`), the class of the object, which the class above brings
` those of its chain's rules `• This` into view for.
. styles [TypeId]
for position in 0 .. < markup-styles.length
    styles += markup-styles[markup-styles.length - 1 - position]
. scopes [RuleScope]
. cells [U32]
. valued [U32]
. context = instances.rows[instance].context
. value-types [TypeId]
if context != U32.max
    . held = instances.contexts[context]
    for position in held.scope-first .. < held.scope-first + held.scopes
        scopes += instances.context-scopes[position]
        cells += instances.context-cells[position]
        valued += instances.context-valued[position]
    for position in held.value-first .. < held.value-first + held.values
        value-types += instances.context-value-types[position]
. made = if context != U32.max then instances.contexts[context].made else no-type
if made == no-type && scoping-named(program.store-atom("This"))
    made = frame.self-type
= instances.intern-context
    - styles
    - markup-sheets
    - sheet-levels
    - scopes
    - cells
    - made
    - 0
    - valued
    - value-types

────────────────────
_ use-cells U32
    - use ScopeUse

` How many state cells of the `when`s around a rule written in a rule seen are carried with it:
` none where it is under none, or under one not carried.
if use.cell >= U32.max - 1 then 0 else 1 + facts.link-count(use.outer-cells)

────────────────────
_ do content-values U32
    - scope RuleScope
    - place U32

` The values of the rule around a rule written in a rule that the function that builds content a
` style rule generates keeps, from the `place`th on among those its context names, made once, in
` the order kept; the markup element it is generated at gives them (`StyleContent`). `U32.max - 1`,
` values not here, where their types are not known.
. frame = valued-frame(scope.frames)
. count U32
for index in 0 .. < facts.scope-values.length
    . held = facts.scope-values[index]
    if held.instance == instance && held.kept != U32.max
        if held.argument == place
            = index as U32
        count += 1
if frame == U32.max
    = U32.max - 1
. taken = frame-types(frame)
if !taken
    = U32.max - 1
. first = facts.scope-value-types.length as U32
for type in taken
    facts.scope-value-types += type
facts.scope-values += ScopeValues
    - instance
    - 0
    - module
    - frame
    - place
    - count
    - U32.max
    - first
    - taken.length as U32
= (facts.scope-values.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
+ do demand-outlet-states Bool

` The functions of the style runtime a slot outlet calls to hold state cells while what it mounts
` is built, and the one that reads them, typed once.
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.outlet-state != no-instance
    = true
. cell = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleScopeState")
if cell == invalid-type
    = false
types.complete(cell)
. module-id = class-ref(types, cell).module
. mark = scratch.types.mark
runtime.outlet-mark = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-outlet-states-mark")
    - mark
if runtime.outlet-mark == no-instance
    = false
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(cell)
runtime.outlet-push = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-outlet-state-push")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(instances.signatures[runtime.outlet-mark].returns)
runtime.outlet-release = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-outlet-states-release")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
runtime.outlet-state = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-outlet-state")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= outlets-ready && runtime.outlet-state != no-instance
    .. outlets-ready = runtime.outlet-push != no-instance && runtime.outlet-release != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do slot-scopes-for Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - class TypeId
    - scopes [ScopeUse]

` The rules written in rules that the functions building what the lines of a markup element's
` body give the slots of its class see before those found on the way to each slot's outlet, as
` the reference's `slotOutletStyleContext` holds them: those the element sees, those its rules
` bring (`scopes-of`), and those of the rules `• This` of its class's chain, under state cells
` made at the element, but those that reach only the markup of its class's own
` (`scope-pending`). False where they are not known here.
if !scoping-any() || !scopes-known() || !sheets-known()
    = false
for use in rule-scopes
    scopes += use
. (start, end) = scopes-of(element)
for position in start .. < end
    if scoped-rows[position].scope.own != .scope-pending
        scopes += scoped-rows[position]
default-scopes(class, element, scopes, false)
= true

────────────────────
+ do slot-outlet (TypeId, SyntaxId)
    - class TypeId
    - name Atom

` The class of a chain whose markup declares the slot of a name, and its outlet there or the line
` that forwards it, as `level-slots` finds them; or no type.
. level TypeId? = class
while level && types.intrinsic-of(level) == .class
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
    . content SyntaxId = 0
    do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(row)
            content = row.content
    if content != 0
        for node in owner.tree.subtree-start(content) .. < content
            do match? owner.tree.nodes[node]
                | .node-slot-outlet(row)
                    . named = program.store-atom("")
                    if row.name != 0
                        named = owner.tree.identifier-name(row.name) ?? named
                    if named == name && !owner.tree.inner-outlet(content, node)
                        = (level, node)
                | .node-markup-slot-forward(row)
                    if owner.tree.identifier-name(row.slot-binding) == name
                        = (level, node)
    level = types.base-of(level)
= (no-type, 0u32)

────────────────────
+ do outlet-scopes U32
    - class TypeId
    - name Atom
    - content TypeId
    - applies Bool
    - base [ScopeUse]
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - levels [U32]
    - found [ScopeUse]
    - keeps-own Bool

` The rules written in rules that the function building what a line gives a slot of a class, of
` type `content`, sees after those of the markup that gives it (`base`, seeing the style sheets
` `sheets` in their `levels`), found on the way to the slot's outlet, as the reference's
` `markupSlotOutletRuleScopes` finds them (`follow-outlet`), the state cell of the `when` around
` each one the cell that outlet holds of those made there (`discovering`); then, where it
` `applies` them, as `markupSlotScopeAdditions` does, those the rules the outlet applies bring
` (`outlet-applications`). None are found on the way to an outlet being followed already. Answers
` 0, 2 where one is declined, or 3 where the rules the outlet applies bring rules under the state
` cells of `when`s, which the function that builds the content brings itself
` (`root-applications`); `found` is given those found for 0, and those but these for 3. The way
` sees of `base` those that match in the markup of the class being filled (`scope-entered`) only
` where that markup `keeps-own`, as the class's chain does, as the reference's
` `markupSlotScopeAdditions` leaves them, and none found reaches only the markup of an element's
` class (`scope-pending`), which what a line gives a slot is not.
. (owner, outlet) = slot-outlet(class, name)
if owner == no-type
    = 0
. ref = class-ref(types, owner)
. tag = ((ref.module as U64) /lshift/ 32) /or/ (outlet as U64)
. followed = discoveries.find(tag) != null
. written = program.modules[ref.module].tree
. markup SyntaxId = 0
do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        markup = declared.content
. root = written.root-this(markup)
. path [SyntaxId]
. node = written.holder-of(outlet)
while node != 0 && node != markup
    if node != root && written.nodes[node] is .node-markup
        path += node
    node = written.holder-of(node)
. saved-scopes [ScopeUse]
for use in rule-scopes
    saved-scopes += use
. saved-sheets [TypeId]
for sheet in markup-sheets
    saved-sheets += sheet
. saved-levels [U32]
for level in sheet-levels
    saved-levels += level
. own-keying = keying
rule-scopes.clear()
for use in base
    if keeps-own || use.scope.own != .scope-entered
        rule-scopes += use
. based = rule-scopes.length
markup-sheets.clear()
sheet-levels.clear()
for sheet in sheets
    markup-sheets += sheet
for level in levels
    sheet-levels += level
keying = keying.sheet-self = owner
keying = keying.discovering = true
. status = 1u32
if !followed
    discoveries += tag
    status = follow-outlet(owner, ref.module, written, root, path, outlet, name)
    discoveries.pop()
if status == 3
    status = 2
if status == 1
    status = 0
    while rule-scopes.length > based
        rule-scopes.pop()
if status == 0 && applies
    markup-sheets.clear()
    sheet-levels.clear()
    for sheet in sheets
        markup-sheets += sheet
    for level in levels
        sheet-levels += level
    status = outlet-applications(class, name, content)
if status == 0 || status == 3
    for position in based .. < rule-scopes.length
        if rule-scopes[position].scope.own != .scope-pending
            found += rule-scopes[position]
rule-scopes.clear()
for use in saved-scopes
    rule-scopes += use
markup-sheets.clear()
for sheet in saved-sheets
    markup-sheets += sheet
sheet-levels.clear()
for level in saved-levels
    sheet-levels += level
keying = own-keying
= status

────────────────────
_ do follow-outlet U32
    - owner TypeId
    - home ModuleId
    - written AST
    - root SyntaxId
    - path [SyntaxId]
    - outlet SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` Follows the way to a slot outlet of the markup written in the class `owner`, in `home`, through
` the markup elements `path` it is in, innermost first, bringing into view the rules written in
` rules seen on the way (`rule-scopes`), as `markupSlotOutletRuleScopes` does: where the class
` above writes markup, those of its root `<This` and those found on the way to the outlet of the
` slot the outermost element gives content, or the default one; else those of the class's root
` `<This` (`gather-root`). Then, for each element, outermost first, those its rules bring; where
` the next is content of a slot of the element's class, or the outlet forwards one of it, those of
` the rules `• This` of its chain, made at the element, and those found on the way to that slot's
` outlet in turn. Answers as `outlet-scopes` does.
. above = types.base-of(owner) ?? no-type
. entered = false
if above != no-type && writes-content(above)
    . first = if path.length != 0 then path[path.length - 1] else 0u32
    . slot = program.store-atom("")
    . bound = false
    do match? written.nodes[first]
        | .node-markup(row)
            if row.slot-binding != 0 && written.holder-of(first) == owner-lines
                bound = true
                slot = written.identifier-name(row.slot-binding) ?? slot
            .. owner-lines = written.content-lines(class-content(owner))
    . names [Atom]
    . wanted [TypeId]
    . items [TypeId]
    if !class-outlets(above, names, wanted, items)
        = 2
    . has = names.find(slot) != null
    if bound && !has
        = 1
    if has
        . base-written = program.modules[class-ref(types, above).module].tree
        . base-content = class-content(above)
        if gather-root(above, base-module, base-written, base-written.root-this(base-content)) != 0
            = 2
        .. base-module = class-ref(types, above).module
        . seen [ScopeUse]
        for use in rule-scopes
            seen += use
        . sheets [TypeId]
        for sheet in markup-sheets
            sheets += sheet
        . levels [U32]
        for level in sheet-levels
            levels += level
        . inner [ScopeUse]
        . status = outlet-scopes
            - above
            - slot
            - wanted[names.find(slot)!]
            - true
            - seen
            - sheets
            - levels
            - inner
            - true
        if status != 0
            = status
        for use in inner
            rule-scopes += use
        entered = true
if !entered && gather-root(owner, home, written, root) != 0
    = 2
. ref = class-ref(types, owner)
. args = RowRange'TypeId()
do match? types.rows[owner]
    | .type-class(row)
        args = row.args
. env = types.class-env-for(ref.module, ref.decl, args, owner)
. status = 0u32
for index in 0 .. < path.length
    . node = path[path.length - 1 - index]
    . next = if index + 1 < path.length then path[path.length - 2 - index] else 0u32
    do match? written.nodes[node]
        | .node-markup(row)
            types.clear-fault()
            . type = types.evaluate-type(home, written, row.type-id, env)
            types.clear-fault()
            if type == invalid-type || type == no-type || types.intrinsic-of(type) != .class
                status = 1
                break
            . names [Atom]
            for text in implicit-names(type, row.type-id, row.id, written)
                names += program.store-atom(text)
            . gathered [ScopeUse]
            . own-keying = keying
            keying = Keying(keying.discovering, keying.sheet-self, home, node)
            . gathering = gather-scopes
                - type
                - names
                - row.style-rule-applications
                - node
                - type
                - gathered
                - written
            keying = own-keying
            if !gathering
                status = 2
                break
            for use in gathered
                rule-scopes += use
            add-sheet-groups(type, markup-sheets, sheet-levels)
            . forwards = written.nodes[outlet] is .node-markup-slot-forward && last-step
                .. last-step = index == path.length - 1
            . bound SyntaxId = 0
            do match? written.nodes[next]
                | .node-markup(line)
                    if line.slot-binding != 0 && row.body != 0 && in-body
                        bound = next
                    .. in-body = written.holder-of(next) == row.body
            . slot = program.store-atom("")
            if forwards
                slot = name
            else if bound != 0
                do match? written.nodes[bound]
                    | .node-markup(line)
                        slot = written.identifier-name(line.slot-binding) ?? slot
            . slots [Atom]
            . wanted [TypeId]
            . items [TypeId]
            if !class-outlets(type, slots, wanted, items)
                status = 2
                break
            . has = slots.find(slot) != null
            if (bound != 0 || forwards) && !has
                status = 1
                break
            if !has
                continue
            . outer-keying = keying
            keying = Keying(keying.discovering, keying.sheet-self, home, node)
            default-scopes(type, node, rule-scopes, false)
            keying = outer-keying
            . seen [ScopeUse]
            for use in rule-scopes
                seen += use
            . sheets [TypeId]
            for sheet in markup-sheets
                sheets += sheet
            . levels [U32]
            for level in sheet-levels
                levels += level
            . inner [ScopeUse]
            . held = outlet-scopes
                - type
                - slot
                - wanted[slots.find(slot)!]
                - !forwards
                - seen
                - sheets
                - levels
                - inner
                - false
            if held != 0
                status = held
                break
            for use in inner
                rule-scopes += use
types.env-release(env)
= status

────────────────────
_ do gather-root U32
    - class TypeId
    - home ModuleId
    - written AST
    - root SyntaxId

` Brings into view, on the way to a slot outlet, the rules written in rules that the rules a root
` `<This` of the markup a class writes matches bring, each not in view already, as the reference's
` `classContentRootStyleRuleScopes` gathers them, the state cell of each made where the root is.
` Answers 0, or 2 where one is declined.
do match? written.nodes[root]
    | .node-markup(row)
        . names [Atom]
        for text in implicit-names(class, row.type-id, 0, written)
            names += program.store-atom(text)
        . gathered [ScopeUse]
        . own-keying = keying
        keying = Keying(keying.discovering, keying.sheet-self, home, root)
        . gathering = gather-scopes
            - class
            - names
            - row.style-rule-applications
            - root
            - class
            - gathered
            - written
        keying = own-keying
        if !gathering
            = 2
        . added [ScopeUse]
        for use in gathered
            . shown = false
            for held in rule-scopes
                shown = shown || instances.same-scope(held.scope, use.scope)
            for held in added
                shown = shown || instances.same-scope(held.scope, use.scope)
            if !shown
                added += use
        for use in added
            rule-scopes += use
= 0

────────────────────
+ do class-content SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` The section of markup a class writes, or none.
. ref = class-ref(types, class)
do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        = declared.content
= 0

────────────────────
_ do content-cell U32
    - scope RuleScope
    - kept U32
    - depth U32

` The state cell the function that builds generated content keeps, its `kept`th, for a `when`
` around a rule written in a rule its context gives: the frame of the rule that is the `depth`th
` `when`'s from the innermost, which the markup element the content is generated at holds
` (`StyleContent`).
. frame = scope.frames
. passed U32
while frame != U32.max
    if instances.frames[frame].gate != 0
        if passed == depth
            break
        passed += 1
    frame = instances.frames[frame].outer
. module = if frame != U32.max then instances.frames[frame].module else 0u32
. branch = if frame != U32.max then instances.frames[frame].gate else 0u32
facts.scope-cells += ScopeCell
    - instance
    - U32.max
    - module
    - branch
    - no-type
    - true
    - U32.max
    - U32.max
    - kept
= (facts.scope-cells.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
_ do record-scopes
    - id SyntaxId
    - scopes [ScopeUse]

` Keeps the rules written in rules that the style rules a markup element applies bring into view,
` for the markup its object makes and its body.
scoped-sites += id
scoped-starts += scoped-rows.length as U32
for scope in scopes
    scoped-rows += scope
scoped-ends += scoped-rows.length as U32

────────────────────
_ do push-scopes
    - id SyntaxId

` Brings into view, for the constructor of a markup element's object, the rules written in rules
` that the style rules the element applies do, those that reach only the markup of its class's
` own (`scope-pending`) with them.
. (start, end) = scopes-of(id)
for position in start .. < end
    rule-scopes += scoped-rows[position]

────────────────────
_ do push-body-scopes
    - id SyntaxId

` Brings into view, for the markup in a markup element's body, the rules written in rules that the
` style rules the element applies do, but those that reach only the markup of its class's own
` (`scope-pending`), as the reference's `withoutPendingOwnStyleRuleScopes` leaves them out.
. (start, end) = scopes-of(id)
for position in start .. < end
    if scoped-rows[position].scope.own != .scope-pending
        rule-scopes += scoped-rows[position]

────────────────────
+ do markup-layer U32

` The layer at which the elements of markup written here declare styles: content, 1, in the
` function that makes a class's content, as the reference sets it there, and inline, 5,
` anywhere else. A function that builds markup takes that of the markup around it
` (`layer-given`), as the reference's builders carry it. None in another function nested in one
` that makes content, which the reference gives the layer of the function it is made in only in
` some ways of making it.
if layer-given != 0
    = layer-given
if frame.declaration.is-content
    = 1
. outer = instances.rows[instance].enclosing
while outer != no-instance
    . row = instances.rows[outer]
    . written = describe(program, row.module, row.decl)
    if written && written.is-content
        = U32.max
    outer = row.enclosing
= 5

────────────────────
+ do reads-element Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - tree AST
    - value SyntaxId

` Whether a value reads by its name alone a property the markup of a class declares for an
` element, apart from in the functions written in it.
. floor = tree.subtree-start(value)
. node = value + 1
while node > floor
    node -= 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-function-syntax
            node = tree.subtree-start(node)
        | .node-identifier(row)
            . place = property-named(receiver, row.name)
            if place && names-element(types, types.properties[place])
                = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do writes-content Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a class, or one above it, has a section of markup.
. level TypeId? = type
while level
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
    do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            do match? owner.decls[class.content-function]
                | .decl-function(fn)
                    if fn.is-content && fn.syntax != 0
                        = true
    level = types.base-of(level)
= false

────────────────────
+ do check-markup-trigger
    - receiver TypeId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - rule ASTWheneverRule

` A `whenever` rule on the markup an object is in, typed as the reference compiles it: the
` object must be a markup host, and so must the class the rule looks for, which, for an
` ancestor, must declare no `==`, since a new ancestor is compared with the last as one object,
` which an optional of the class holds.
` Children and descendants are looked for by the number of the class among the targets of
` descendant queries; a class numbered only as the rule is typed, as one a class with type
` parameters looks for is, has no shape here. Where the rule names its changes, a
` `MarkupChangeSet` of that class is made for it, whose lists take each object added or
` removed and which is emptied after each run. The rule registers with the markup runtime,
` finds parent hosts there, and runs its live action by a call; its body runs in that action.
` The reference's errors for these, and runtime functions that raise, have no shape here.
. ancestor = rule.kind.text == "ancestor"
. host = if is-markup-host(receiver) then markup-host else no-type
    .. markup-host = derived-interface(receiver, types.markup-host-decl)
. target = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, rule.target-type, frame.env)
if host == no-type || target == invalid-type || !is-markup-host(target)
    decline(syntax)
    =
if ancestor
    for token in ["==", "!="]
        if calls.has-operator(target, program.store-atom(token), target)
            decline(syntax)
            =
. found = if ancestor then types.optional-of(target) else no-type
if found != no-type
    types.complete(found)
. trigger = MarkupTrigger
    - instance
    - target
    - 0
    - found
    - host
    - no-type
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
if !ancestor
    note-class-targets(receiver)
    . found = facts.query-targets.find(target)
    if !found
        decline(syntax)
        =
    trigger.target-id = (found + 1) as U32
demand-live-runtime()
. markup = types.markup-host-decl.module
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for arg in tree.children[rule.args]
    . named SyntaxId = 0
    do match? tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument-decl(row)
            do match? tree.nodes[row.pattern]
                | .node-identifier
                    named = row.pattern
                | .node-type-capture(capture)
                    named = if capture.type == 0 then capture.id else 0
    . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, named)
    . name = tree.identifier-atom(named) if named != 0
    trigger.changes = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupChangeSet", target)
    . added = property-named(trigger.changes, program.store-atom("added")) if trigger.changes != invalid-type
    if !name || name.text != "changes" || resolution.kind != .resolve-slot || !added
        decline(arg)
        =
    frame.assign(resolution.slot, trigger.changes)
    trigger.made = calls.demand-constructor(trigger.changes, mark)
    trigger.clear = calls.demand-method(trigger.changes, program.store-atom("clear"))
    scratch.types.push(target)
    trigger.record = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - markup
        - types.properties[added].type
        - program.store-atom("+=")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if rule.kind.text != "descendants"
    scratch.types.push(host)
    trigger.parent = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - markup
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("markup-query-parent-host")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
. callback = types.well-known-type
    - "core/markup"
    - if ancestor then "MarkupAncestorQueryRefresher" else "MarkupDescendantsQueryApplier"
scratch.types.push(host)
if !ancestor
    scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
    scratch.types.push(callback)
scratch.types.push(callback)
trigger.register = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - markup
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom
        - if ancestor then "register-markup-ancestor-query" else "register-markup-descendants-query"
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
trigger.schedule = if types.call-atom then calls.demand-method(types.live-action-type, types.call-atom) else no-instance
for callee in [trigger.made, trigger.clear, trigger.record, trigger.parent, trigger.register, trigger.schedule]
    if callee != no-instance
        demand-errors(callee)
. orphaned = trigger.parent == no-instance && rule.kind.text != "descendants"
. missing = orphaned || trigger.register == no-instance || trigger.schedule == no-instance
. unmade = trigger.changes != no-type && (set-missing || trigger.record == no-instance)
    .. set-missing = trigger.made == no-instance || trigger.clear == no-instance
if missing || unmade || callback == invalid-type
    decline(syntax)
    =
for callee in [trigger.made, trigger.clear, trigger.record, trigger.parent, trigger.register, trigger.schedule]
    if callee != no-instance && instances.signatures[callee].errors.count != 0
        decline(syntax)
        =
facts.markup-triggers += trigger
check-statement(rule.body)

────────────────────
+ do follows-content Bool
    - member SyntaxId
    - owner DeclId

` Whether a section written in a class follows the class's content: an earlier section, or a
` `• This` with lines that are not its own (`rule-part`), which the reference makes the content.
` The reference reports a second as it declares the class, used or not.
if !(tree.nodes[member] is .node-content-block)
    = false
do match? program.modules[module].decls[owner]
    | .decl-class(class)
        do match? tree.nodes[class.syntax]
            | .node-class-block(row)
                for written in tree.children[row.members]
                    if written == member
                        = false
                    if tree.nodes[written] is .node-content-block || tree.holds-markup(written)
                        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do check-content
    - decl DeclId
    - class ClassDecl

` A section of a type with markup written in it is the type's content, which only a class
` holds. A struct says that it holds none; in a type of any other kind the section is declined.
` A root `<This` is checked as the reference checks it.
if class.content == 0
    =
if class.or-bases.count != 0
    decline(class.content)
    =
if class.base != 0
    . env = types.class-env(module, decl)
    . base = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, class.base, env)
    types.env-release(env)
    if base == invalid-type
        =
    . kind = types.intrinsic-of(base)
    if kind == .struct
        . message = program.store-atom("Content is not supported on structs")
        frame.diagnose(class.syntax, .stated, message)
        =
    if kind != .class
        decline(class.content)
        =
check-root(decl, class)

────────────────────
_ do check-root
    - decl DeclId
    - class ClassDecl

` The root `<This` of the markup written in a class names no object, takes no argument and fills no
` slot, and every other line of the markup is written in it, but state machines. Each of its lines
` that assigns gives a property the class has from a class above its first value: a property stored
` in the object, given one value. One the class declares itself with a value is given two; one it
` declares with none takes this one. A name that is no property is one of a style, where a style
` could answer it, which the constructor declares (`apply-root-rules`), and else is no name at all.
` The style rules it applies are applied by the constructor (`apply-root-rules`), and are declined
` where the program has no style runtime.
. root = tree.root-this(class.content)
do match? tree.nodes[root]
    | .node-markup(row)
        if row.id != 0
            frame.diagnose(row.id, .stated, program.store-atom("Root <This> cannot have an id"))
            =
        if row.slot-binding != 0
            frame.diagnose
                - row.slot-binding
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom("Root <This> cannot bind a slot")
            =
        if row.args.count != 0
            . message = program.store-atom("Root <This> cannot pass constructor arguments")
            frame.diagnose(tree.children[row.args.start], .stated, message)
            =
        if row.slot-parameter != 0 || (row.style-rule-applications.count != 0 && no-style-module)
            decline(root)
            =
        .. no-style-module = !program.module-by-name("core/style")
        do match? tree.nodes[class.content]
            | .node-content-block(section)
                do match? tree.nodes[section.body]
                    | .node-block(block)
                        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
                            if statement == root || tree.nodes[statement] is .node-state-machine
                                continue
                            . message = program.store-atom
                                - "Root <This> must wrap all class content"
                            frame.diagnose(root, .stated, message)
                            =
        . mark = scratch.types.mark
        . owner = types.class-pattern-with-args(module, decl, mark)
        if owner == invalid-type
            =
        types.complete(owner)
        . seen [Atom]
        do match? tree.nodes[row.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in tree.children[block.body]
                    do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                        | .node-assign(attribute)
                            . name = style-name(tree, attribute.lhs)
                            if attribute.op == .bind-op
                                . message = "A root <This> cannot bind with \"<->\", since its attributes give the object's own properties their first values; bind the property where the object is made"
                                frame.diagnose(statement, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
                                =
                            if !name || attribute.op != .eq-op
                                decline(statement)
                                =
                            . place = property-named(owner, name)
                            if !place
                                if program.module-by-name("core/style")
                                    continue
                                frame.diagnose
                                    - attribute.lhs
                                    - .stated
                                    - program.store-atom("Property not found")
                                =
                            if seen.find(name) != null
                                . message = program.store-atom
                                    - "Duplicate root <This> property default"
                                frame.diagnose(attribute.lhs, .stated, message)
                                =
                            seen += name
                            if types.properties[place].storage-kind != .storage-eager
                                . message = program.store-atom
                                    - "Root <This> can only default eager properties"
                                frame.diagnose(attribute.lhs, .stated, message)
                                =
                            . own = owner-property(program, module, decl, name)
                            do match? program.modules[module].decls[own]
                                | .decl-property(property)
                                    if own != 0 && !property.defaults-root && property.value != 0
                                        . message = "Root <This> property default duplicates property declaration"
                                        frame.diagnose
                                            - attribute.lhs
                                            - .stated
                                            - program.store-atom(message)
                                        =

────────────────────
+ is-region-body Bool
    - decl DeclId

match program.modules[module].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        fn.kind == .region-decl
    ??
        false

────────────────────
+ awaits-element Bool
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a local an enclosing function declares is the name of a markup element it has not
` made yet. A closure made before then reads it when it runs (`read-later-element`).
|? outer && frame.is-captured(slot)
    outer.awaits-element(slot)
??
    waited != null && awaited[waited] != 0

.. waited = unbuilt.find(slot)

────────────────────
_ do starts-task Bool
    - slot SlotId

. enclosing = outer
if !enclosing || !frame.is-captured(slot)
    = false
= enclosing.starts-task(slot) || (frame.declaration.kind == .task-decl && !enclosing.frame.is-captured(slot))

────────────────────
_ do foresee-element TypeId
    - slot SlotId

if outer && frame.is-captured(slot)
    = outer.foresee-element(slot)
. known = foreseen.find(slot)
if known != null
    = foreseen-types[known]
. waited = unbuilt.find(slot)
if waited == null || awaited[waited] == 0
    = no-type
do match? tree.nodes[awaited[waited]]
    | .node-markup(row)
        types.clear-fault()
        . class = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, frame.env)
        types.clear-fault()
        if class != invalid-type
            foreseen += slot
            foreseen-types += class
        = class
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do assign-element
    - slot SlotId
    - made TypeId
    - element SyntaxId

frame.assign(slot, made)
. known = foreseen.find(slot)
if known == null || made == invalid-type || foreseen-types[known] == made
    =
. name = bindings.slots[slot].name
. read = type-source(types, foreseen-types[known])
. message = "Named markup element \"${name.text}\" is read in a closure made before its markup constructs it, as $read, but its markup makes ${type-source(types, made)}; write its type in full"
frame.diagnose(element, .stated, program.store-atom(message))

────────────────────
+ do infer-markup-read Found
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTMarkupReadExpression

` A read of a markup link, `%parent`, `%first-child`, `%last-child`, `%previous-sibling` or
` `%next-sibling`, of an object or of `this` whose class is a markup host: the optional of the
` host the markup runtime links it to. Where the class is a tree host of a concrete class of
` children, a child read gives that class, and so do a parent and a sibling read where the
` subject is one; else a sibling read gives the subject's class, and any other the host. The
` link is the host's object taken as that class, unchecked, as the reference takes it. A read
` written after `?` reads from what the optional before it holds, as a read of a member does. A
` link given as an interface has no shape here.
. name = row.name.text
. reader = "markup-structural-${name}-host"
if name != "parent" && name != "first-child" && name != "last-child" && no-sibling
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Markup link \"%$name\" not found"))
    = Found(invalid-type)
.. no-sibling = name != "previous-sibling" && name != "next-sibling"
. subject = no-type
if row.object != 0
    if this.tree.optional-chain-expr(row.object) != 0
        decline(id)
        = Found(invalid-type)
    . object-found = infer-found(row.object)
    . object = object-found.type
    . own = object-found.link
    if object == invalid-type
        = Found(invalid-type)
    . form = if row.is-optional then note-chain(id, id, object) else ChainForm.chain-plain
    if form == .chain-absent || absent-after(row.object, object)
        = Found(types.null-type)
    . optional = form == .chain-tested
    subject = link-receiver(row.object, object, own, optional)
    if optional
        facts.unwrapped.append(UnwrappedFact(instance, row.object, subject))
else
    subject = frame.self-type
if subject == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Markup link \"%$name\" not found"))
    = Found(invalid-type)
if types.is-optional(subject)
    decline(id)
    = Found(invalid-type)
. host-decl = types.markup-host-decl
. host = if hostable then derived-interface(subject, host-decl) else no-type
    .. hostable = subject != no-type && (host-decl.module != 0 || host-decl.decl != 0)
if host == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Markup link \"%$name\" not found"))
    = Found(invalid-type)
if types.intrinsic-of(subject) != .class && subject != host
    decline(id)
    = Found(invalid-type)
. tree = if tree-host then derived-interface(subject, types.markup-tree-host-decl) else no-type
    .. tree-host = types.markup-tree-host-decl.module != 0 || types.markup-tree-host-decl.decl != 0
. child = if tree != no-type then first-arg(tree) else no-type
. concrete = child != no-type && !types.completions[child].has-variables
. target = no-type
if name == "first-child" || name == "last-child"
    target = if concrete then child else no-type
else if concrete && derived-interface(subject, class-ref(types, child)) == child
    target = child
else if name == "previous-sibling" || name == "next-sibling"
    target = if !types.completions[subject].has-variables then subject else no-type
if target == host
    target = no-type
if target != no-type && types.intrinsic-of(target) != .class
    decline(id)
    = Found(invalid-type)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(host)
. read = calls.demand-runtime-call(host-decl.module, no-type, program.store-atom(reader), mark)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if read == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = Found(invalid-type)
conversions.convert(id, if row.object != 0 then row.object else id, subject, host, .reason-argument)
facts.markup-reads += MarkupRead(instance, id, read, target)
. link = types.optional-of(if target != no-type then target else host)
= Found(link).linking(link)

────────────────────
+ do infer-markup TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTMarkup
    - want Want = Want()

` A markup element: an object of its class, whose body runs with each of its lines as
` content of the object. A line that gives a value is taken by the element: by its `+=`, or
` else by its `++=`. An `if` and a `for` written as lines run their bodies as content of the
` same element; a `do` block runs as it would anywhere. The object of an element a block
` declares a name for was made where that block starts, and the name holds it, but where the
` name is placed (`is-placed`): the object is made here and the name given it, which a
` function written in another may not do. An element written with a name no block declares,
` where the name is one something else declared, is that thing's value to the reference and
` makes no object: it is declined, but where that is the property the markup of the class
` declares for the element (`names-content-property`), whose object is made here and given to
` the property once the line has run. A name placed so that the function building a slot an
` element is given declares it in a function the slot is written in is given the object
` there, as the reference's builder writes the local it captures (`places-across`). What
` makes a placed element reads its name only in a function of its own: read anywhere else, the
` name is the reference's error. An
` element that binds a slot is made only by the function
` that builds the slot; written as a line anywhere else it is the reference's error. An
` element of a markup host runs under the batch of markup in force, as `batch-element` says.
if row.slot-binding != 0 && !builds-slot(id)
    if want.asks(.want-content-line)
        frame.diagnose
            - row.slot-binding
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom("A slot is filled by a line of the element's body, or by a line of an arm of an if or match there")
    else
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. slot = element-slot(id, row.id)
if row.id != 0 && !slot
    . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, row.id)
    . found = resolution.kind != .resolve-unresolved && resolution.kind != .resolve-none
    if (found && !names-content-property(id, row.id)) || received
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    .. received = (resolution.flags /and/ ResolutionFlag.resolution-received) != 0
. placed = slot && bindings.is-placed(slot)
if placed && frame.is-captured(slot!) && !places-across(slot!)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. made = if slot && !placed then frame.slot-type(slot) else no-type
if slot && !placed && made == no-type
    . name = bindings.slots[slot].name
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("The compiler made no object for the markup element named \"${name.text}\" where the body that names it starts"))
    = invalid-type
if placed
    . first = unbuilt.length
    . around = building
    unbuilt += slot!
    awaited += 0
    building = slot!
    made = make-element(id, row)
    building = around
    while unbuilt.length > first
        unbuilt.pop()
        awaited.pop()
else if !slot
    made = make-element(id, row)
if made == invalid-type || made == no-type
    = invalid-type
if placed
    assign-placed(slot!, made)
if !keep-element(id, made)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. rooted = batch-element(id, row, made, want.asks(.want-content-line))
if row.body != 0 && !wraps-default(row.body)
    . styled = markup-styles.length
    if program.module-by-name("core/style") && !add-visible-styles(made, markup-styles, id)
        = invalid-type
    . sheeted = markup-sheets.length
    if program.module-by-name("core/style")
        if markup-sheets.length == 0
            add-sheet-groups(frame.self-type, markup-sheets, sheet-levels)
        add-sheet-groups(made, markup-sheets, sheet-levels)
    . scoped = rule-scopes.length
    push-body-scopes(id)
    content-blocks += row.body
    content-parents += made
    content-names += false
    element-bodies += row.body
    batched += rooted
    check-statement(row.body)
    batched.pop()
    content-blocks.pop()
    content-parents.pop()
    content-names.pop()
    element-bodies.pop()
    while rule-scopes.length > scoped
        rule-scopes.pop()
    while markup-styles.length > styled
        markup-styles.pop()
    while markup-sheets.length > sheeted
        markup-sheets.pop()
        sheet-levels.pop()
= made

────────────────────
_ do batch-element Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTMarkup
    - made TypeId
    - linked Bool

` Whether a batch of markup is in force in the body of a markup element: the element itself
` where its class is a batch, else the one in force where the element is written. An element
` of a markup host under one whose body gives it content (`gives-default`) is put under the
` batch by the markup runtime's `ensure-markup-root` before its body runs, and one that is no
` line of another element is mounted as a root of the batch by `markup-mount-root` once it is
` made, as the reference does, but for one the function that builds a row of a markup loop
` region or what a line gives a slot makes, which the reference builds with both put off. An
` element that is a batch is converted to the `MarkupRootElement` what is made under it is put under.
. owns = is-batch(made)
. rooted = owns || in-batch()
if !rooted
    = false
. root = ElementRoot(instance, id, no-instance, no-instance, owns)
. batch = batch-type()
if owns
    conversions.convert(row.type-id, row.type-id, made, batch, .reason-markup-batch)
. bodied = gives-default(row.body)
if is-markup-host(made) && !defers-roots() && (bodied || !linked)
    . markup = types.markup-host-decl.module
    . host = derived-interface(made, types.markup-host-decl)
    . optional = types.optional-of(batch)
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    scratch.types.push(host)
    scratch.types.push(optional)
    if bodied
        root.ensure = calls.demand-runtime-call
            - markup
            - no-type
            - program.store-atom("ensure-markup-root")
            - mark
    if !linked
        root.mount = calls.demand-runtime-call
            - markup
            - no-type
            - program.store-atom("markup-mount-root")
            - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if (bodied && root.ensure == no-instance) || (!linked && root.mount == no-instance)
        decline(id)
        = rooted
    conversions.convert(row.type-id, row.type-id, made, host, .reason-markup-host)
    conversions.convert(row.type-id, row.type-id, batch, optional, .reason-markup-root)
if owns || root.ensure != no-instance || root.mount != no-instance
    facts.element-roots += root
= rooted

────────────────────
_ defers-roots Bool

` Whether the function being typed builds markup with its roots neither put under the batch in
` force nor mounted: one that builds a row of a markup loop region or what a line gives a slot,
` as the reference builds them.
frame.declaration.kind == .row-decl || frame.declaration.kind == .slot-decl

────────────────────
+ do make-element TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTMarkup

` The object of a markup element, made by the constructor its arguments choose. An argument
` whose parameter has the name of a property of the class is stored in that property once
` the object is made, as the reference binds the two.
` An attribute whose value reads something tracked is given again by a function of its own.
` An attribute that names a property of a style the element sees is a style declaration
` (`declare-styles`), after the style rules the element applies (`apply-style-rules`). An
` element whose body gives slots content gives its constructor the functions that build them
` (`supply-slots`). The constructor of a class whose markup is its content is one of its own
` for the styles and style sheets the element sees (`element-context`). The rules written in
` rules that the element's style rules bring into view are gathered first, for the class
` written, as the reference prepares them (`gather-scopes`); an element whose object is of
` another class is declined then. One whose class takes its content through the markup protocol
` or builds content of its own is declined, and so is a body that tracks what it reads
` elsewhere. The local that keeps the object for the functions of its body that read its members
` holds the class written while the body is typed (`keep-element`).
if !is-plain-body(row.body)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
types.clear-fault()
. class = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, frame.env)
if class == invalid-type
    if !report-circular() && !report-fault(row.type-id)
        frame.diagnose(row.type-id, .stated, program.store-atom("Type not found"))
    = invalid-type
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
. scoping = may-scope(class, row)
if scoping
    . names [Atom]
    for name in implicit-names(class, row.type-id, row.id, tree)
        names += program.store-atom(name)
    . gathered [ScopeUse]
    if !gather-scopes(class, names, row.style-rule-applications, id, class, gathered, tree)
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    record-scopes(id, gathered)
. names-mark = scratch.names.mark
. builders-mark = scratch.types.mark
if !supply-slots(id, row.body, class)
    scratch.names.rewind(names-mark)
    scratch.types.rewind(builders-mark)
    = invalid-type
. slots = scratch.names.since(names-mark)
. builders = scratch.types.since(builders-mark)
. context = element-context(class, id)
if context == U32.max - 1
    scratch.names.rewind(names-mark)
    scratch.types.rewind(builders-mark)
    = invalid-type
do keep-element(id, class)
. made = infer-call(id, row.type-id, RowRange'SyntaxId(), row.args, false, row.body, class, Want(), slots, builders, context).type
scratch.names.rewind(names-mark)
scratch.types.rewind(builders-mark)
if made == invalid-type || made == no-type
    = invalid-type
if !fills-constructor(id, row, made)
    = invalid-type
if !accepts || (tree.has-attributes(row.body) && made != class) || (scoping && made != class)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. accepts = takes-lines(made) || takes-hosted(made) || (holds-slot(made) && is-markup-host(made))
if !check-cells(id, id, made, true)
    = invalid-type
. outer-prepared = preparing
preparing = preparing.site = id
. applied = apply-style-rules(id, made, row)
preparing = outer-prepared
if applied == U32.max || !declare-styles(id, made, row.body, applied)
    = invalid-type
if !store-attributes(id, made, row.args, row.body) || !store-arguments(id, made, row.args)
    if facts.diagnostics.length == reported
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
settle-attributes(row.body, made, row.type-id)
settle-arguments(id, row.args, made, row.type-id)
= made

────────────────────
_ do fills-constructor Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTMarkup
    - made TypeId

. fact = facts.latest-call(instance, id)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].callee == no-instance
    = true
. callee = instances.rows[facts.calls[fact].callee]
do match? program.modules[callee.module].decls[callee.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.kind != .default-constructor-decl
            = true
. given [Atom]
do match? tree.nodes[row.body] if row.body != 0
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-assign(attribute)
                    . name = tree.identifier-name(attribute.lhs)
                    if name
                        given += name
. count = 0
. wanted Atom? = null
. ref = class-ref(types, made)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        if class.members.count != 0
            for member in owner.member-pool[class.members]
                do match? owner.decls[member]
                    | .decl-function(fn)
                        if fn.kind == .constructor-decl && !fn.is-generated
                            count += 1
                            . fills = true
                            for shape in owner.arg-pool[fn.args]
                                if !shape.has-default && ungiven
                                    fills = false
                                    if !wanted
                                        wanted = shape.name
                                .. ungiven = !shape.name || given.find(shape.name) == null
                            if fills
                                = true
if count == 0
    = true
. shown = type-source(types, made)
. message = "Markup element <$shown gives none of the arguments the constructors of $shown require"
if count == 1 && wanted
    message = "Markup element <$shown gives no value for \"${wanted.text}\", which the constructor of $shown requires"
. named = tree.identifier-name(row.id) if row.id != 0
if named
    message = "$message; \"${named.text}\" after <$shown names the element"
frame.diagnose(row.type-id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
= false

────────────────────
_ do settle-attributes
    - body SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - type-id SyntaxId

` Types the function that gives again each attribute of a markup element whose value read
` something tracked, once the element's object is typed, as the reference makes it: the
` local no name reaches that keeps the object for it, declared at the attribute, holds one of
` the element's class, and the action is made as `owner-action` says, or for a style the
` attribute declares is the style runtime's `StyleDynamicAction` of the class. The local holds
` one also where the value read nothing tracked after all, as where a name the module builder
` took for one of a keyed row's is a member of an element around it, and nothing gives it again.
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(row)
        for statement in tree.children[row.body]
            if tree.nodes[statement] is .node-assign && is-live-statement(statement)
                . kept = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, statement)
                if kept.kind == .resolve-slot
                    frame.assign(kept.slot, made)
            . position = facts.live-statements.length
            while position != 0
                position -= 1
                . live = facts.live-statements[position]
                if live.instance != instance || live.site != statement || live.rerun != no-instance
                    continue
                . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, statement)
                if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
                    decline(statement)
                    =
                . styled = facts.style-declaration-of(instance, statement) != null
                . owned InstanceId? = null
                if styled
                    owned = demand-style-gates(made)
                else
                    owned = owner-action(statement, made, type-id)
                if !owned
                    =
                frame.assign(resolution.slot, made)
                . rerun = demand-lambda(intern-nested(nested-decl-of(statement)), scratch.no-types)
                if rerun == no-instance || instances.signatures[rerun].errors.count != 0
                    decline(statement)
                    =
                instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
                facts.live-statements[position] = LiveStatement
                    - instance
                    - statement
                    - rerun
                    - 0
                    - U32.max
                    - owned
                    - !styled && owned != no-instance && owns-batch(made)
                break
            settle-binding(statement)

────────────────────
_ do settle-binding
    - statement SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-assign(row)
        if row.op != .bind-op
            =
        . given = facts.live-statement-of(instance, statement)
        if !given || given.rerun == no-instance
            =
        . rerun = demand-lambda(intern-nested(nested-decl-of(row.lhs)), scratch.no-types)
        if rerun == no-instance || instances.signatures[rerun].errors.count != 0
            decline(statement)
            =
        facts.live-statements += LiveStatement(instance, row.lhs, rerun, 0, U32.max, given.owned, given.rooted)

────────────────────
+ do settle-content
    - statement SyntaxId
    - parent TypeId
    - produced TypeId

` Types the function that gives a line of a markup element's body again where its value read
` something tracked, once the element has taken it, as the reference makes it: an element of a
` markup host that absorbed the value by its `markup-absorb` absorbs it again, and one that took
` it another way replaces what it took (`replace-again`). The local no name reaches that keeps
` the element's object, declared at the line, holds one of the element's class, the one after it
` what the element took, and the action is made as `owner-action` says. A line of the body of an
` arm of a region is given so to what the arm's function is given, converted at the line.
. position = facts.live-statements.length
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    . live = facts.live-statements[position]
    if live.instance != instance || live.site != statement || live.rerun != no-instance
        continue
    . link = facts.content-link-of(instance, statement)
    . kept = line-keeper(statement)
    . absorbed = link != U32.max && is-markup-host(parent) && unappended && link-called
        .. unappended = facts.content-links[link].append == no-instance
        .. link-called = facts.content-links[link].call != no-fact
    . replaced = if absorbed || link == U32.max then no-type else taken-type
        .. taken-type = content-taken(facts.content-links[link], produced)
    if (!absorbed && replaced == no-type) || kept == no-slot
        decline(statement)
        =
    . type-id SyntaxId = statement
    do match? tree.nodes[tree.content-element(statement)]
        | .node-markup(row)
            type-id = row.type-id
    . owned = owner-action(statement, parent, type-id)
    if !owned
        =
    frame.assign(kept, parent)
    frame.assign(kept + 1, if absorbed then types.void-type else replaced)
    . rerun = demand-lambda(intern-nested(nested-decl-of(statement)), scratch.no-types)
    if rerun == no-instance || instances.signatures[rerun].errors.count != 0
        decline(statement)
        =
    instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
    facts.live-statements[position] = LiveStatement
        - instance
        - statement
        - rerun
        - 0
        - U32.max
        - owned
        - owned != no-instance && owns-batch(parent)
