────────────────────
_ content-taken TypeId
    - row ContentLink
    - produced TypeId

` What a markup element took of a line of its body, which a function that gives the line again
` replaces: the node the markup runtime linked for a markup host, else what the element's
` method answered, or the value where it answers nothing, as the reference keeps it.
|? row.call == no-fact
    no-type
|? row.append != no-instance
    instances.argument-type(row.append, 1)
??
    if answered == types.void-type then produced else answered

.. answered = instances.signatures[facts.calls[row.call].callee].returns

────────────────────
_ do owner-action InstanceId?
    - site SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - type-id SyntaxId

` The function that makes the live action a markup element owns where an attribute or an
` argument of it read something tracked, as the reference makes it: where a batch is found
` for the element, as `owns-batch` says, the markup runtime's `make-markup-action`, given the
` batch; else none where the element's actions are plain ones, and for an element of a markup
` host `make-owner-markup-action`, given the element as the host, to which it is converted at
` its type once, however many of its attributes read something tracked. Either may raise. One
` that has no shape here is declined, which is answered with nothing.
. rooted = owns-batch(made)
if owns-plain-actions(made) && !rooted
    = no-instance
. action = action-maker(site, made, rooted)
if !action
    = null
if !rooted && !converts-at(type-id, .reason-markup-host)
    conversions.convert
        - type-id
        - type-id
        - made
        - derived-interface(made, types.markup-host-decl)
        - .reason-markup-host
= action

────────────────────
_ do converts-at Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - reason ConversionReason

` Whether a conversion for a reason is recorded at a node of the instance being typed.
. fact = facts.first-conversion(instance, site)
while fact != no-fact
    if facts.conversions[fact].reason == reason
        = true
    fact = facts.conversions[fact].next
= false

────────────────────
_ do settle-arguments
    - id SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - type-id SyntaxId

` Types the function that gives again each argument of a markup element, given by position,
` whose value read something tracked, once the element's object is typed, as the reference
` makes it: the parameter the argument fills must name a property of the element's class,
` which is the reference's error otherwise, and the local no name reaches that keeps the
` object, declared at the element, holds one of the element's class. The action is made as
` `owner-action` says.
for arg in tree.children[args]
    . position = facts.live-statements.length
    while position != 0
        position -= 1
        . live = facts.live-statements[position]
        if live.instance != instance || live.site != arg || live.rerun != no-instance
            continue
        . name = argument-name(arg, id, instance)
        . place = property-named(made, name) if name
        if !place
            frame.diagnose
                - arg
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom("Tracked markup constructor argument must match a property")
            =
        . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id)
        if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
            decline(arg)
            =
        . owned = owner-action(arg, made, type-id)
        if !owned
            =
        frame.assign(resolution.slot, made)
        . rerun = demand-lambda(intern-nested(nested-decl-of(arg)), scratch.no-types)
        if rerun == no-instance || instances.signatures[rerun].errors.count != 0
            decline(arg)
            =
        instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
        facts.live-statements[position] = LiveStatement
            - instance
            - arg
            - rerun
            - 0
            - place as U32
            - owned
            - owned != no-instance && owns-batch(made)
        break

────────────────────
+ do push-attributes Bool
    - body SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` Types the attributes of a markup element in the order written and pushes each as an
` argument of its constructor's call: one named as the property, marked as a property, of
` the property's type, to which the value is converted as one assigned is. One that may name a
` style property is left to `declare-styles`, and one a setter answers is no argument
` (`setter-attribute`). False where an attribute has no shape or names no property, which is
` reported.
. given = true
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(row)
        for statement in tree.children[row.body]
            do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-assign(attribute)
                    . name = style-name(tree, attribute.lhs)
                    if styles-attribute(attribute.op, class, name)
                        continue
                    if name && attribute-accessor(class, name)
                        if !setter-attribute(statement, attribute.op, attribute.lhs, attribute.rhs, class)
                            given = false
                        continue
                    . type = attribute-type
                        - statement
                        - attribute.op
                        - attribute.lhs
                        - attribute.rhs
                        - class
                    if type == invalid-type
                        given = false
                    else
                        scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(name, false, false, true, false))
                        scratch.types.push(type)
                        scratch.syntax.push(statement)
= given

────────────────────
+ do setter-attribute Bool
    - statement SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - target SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` An attribute of a markup element that a setter answers, which the reference gives the object
` once it is made, as it updates any property the constructor does not fill: the value is typed
` by itself and the setter chosen for it as an assignment to the property chooses one, the
` reference's error where none answers. One of a setter private to another module, one written
` with an assigning operator, and one of a class with type variables are declined.
. name = tree.identifier-name(target)
. found = attribute-accessor(class, name!)
if op == .bind-op
    . shown = type-short-name(types, class)
    . message = "\"<->\" binds a property the element stores, and $shown answers \"${name!.text}\" with a getter or a setter, which a binding cannot follow; bind a property $shown stores"
    frame.diagnose(target, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = false
if op != .eq-op || !found || types.completions[class].has-variables || is-hidden(types.properties[found], name!, .setter-decl)
    decline(statement)
    = false
. given = stored-value(value, infer(value))
if given == invalid-type
    = false
. diagnosed = facts.diagnostics.length
if calls.setter-call(target, target, class, name!, value, given) == invalid-type
    facts.restate
        - diagnosed
        - instance
        - statement
        - .function-not-found
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Setter not found")
    = false
= true

────────────────────
+ do attribute-accessor Index?
    - class TypeId
    - name Atom

. found = property-named(class, name)
if found
    =? found if types.properties[found].storage-kind == .storage-getter
    = null
= interface-accessor(class, name)

────────────────────
+ do attribute-not-found
    - target SyntaxId
    - name Atom

. message = "Property \"${name.text}\" not found; an assignment in an element's body sets the element's property. To assign a local, put it in a do row: \"do ${name.text} = …\""
frame.diagnose(target, .stated, program.store-atom(message))

────────────────────
+ do attribute-type TypeId
    - statement SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - target SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` The type an attribute of a markup element gives its constructor: that of the property it
` names, to which the value written is converted as a value assigned to the property is. A
` bullet list written for a list takes the list's item type, as the reference contextualizes it.
` A name that is no property of the class, or one private to another module, is the
` reference's error where no style could answer it. An attribute a setter answers, one of an
` array and one written with an assigning operator are declined. An event written is wanted as
` the property's type, as `use-event` says.
. name = tree.identifier-name(target)
if (op != .eq-op && op != .bind-op) || !name || types.intrinsic-of(class) != .class || generic
    decline(statement)
    = invalid-type
.. generic = types.completions[class].has-variables
. place = property-named(class, name)
if op == .bind-op && (!place || is-hidden(types.properties[place], name, .setter-decl))
    . message = "\"<->\" binds a property of the element, and ${type-short-name(types, class)} has no property \"${name.text}\""
    frame.diagnose(target, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
if !place || is-hidden(types.properties[place], name, .setter-decl)
    if program.module-by-name("core/style")
        decline(statement)
    else if place
        frame.diagnose(target, .stated, program.store-atom("Property not found"))
    else
        attribute-not-found(target, name)
    = invalid-type
. property = types.properties[place]
if property.storage-kind == .storage-getter
    decline(statement)
    = invalid-type
. declared = property.type
if declared == no-type
    declared = demand-member(property, class, name)
if declared == no-type || declared == invalid-type
    decline(statement)
    = invalid-type
if is-array-value(declared)
    decline(statement)
    = invalid-type
expect-bullets(value, declared)
. written = infer-with-expected(value, declared, Want().escaping(declared, value))
if written == invalid-type || written == no-type
    = invalid-type
if conversions.convert(statement, value, written, declared, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
= declared

────────────────────
_ do store-attributes Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` Keeps, for each attribute of a markup element that names no parameter of its constructor,
` that the value is stored in the property again once the object is made, as the reference
` does, or given to the setter that answers it. An attribute that names a parameter an
` argument fills is the reference's error. One that names another parameter fills it, as an
` argument by name does, and is not stored again; one a setter answers that names a parameter
` is declined.
. fact = facts.latest-call(instance, id)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].callee == no-instance
    = !tree.has-attributes(body)
. call = facts.calls[fact]
. callee = instances.rows[call.callee]
. owner = program.modules[callee.module]
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(row)
        do match? owner.decls[callee.decl]
            | .decl-function(fn)
                . given U32
                . setters U32
                for statement in tree.children[row.body]
                    do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                        | .node-assign(attribute)
                            . name = tree.identifier-name(attribute.lhs)
                            . place = (property-named(made, name) ?? interface-accessor(made, name)) if name
                            if !place && facts.style-declaration-of(instance, statement)
                                continue
                            if !place
                                = false
                            . parameter = shape-index(owner, fn, name!)
                            if types.properties[place].storage-kind == .storage-getter
                                if parameter != U32.max
                                    decline(statement)
                                    = false
                                facts.note-element-store
                                    - ElementStore(instance, id, setters, U32.max, 0, attribute.lhs)
                                setters += 1
                                continue
                            if parameter != U32.max
                                . fill = if in-fills then kept else ArgumentFill.fill-empty
                                    .. in-fills = parameter < call.fills.count
                                    .. kept = facts.call-fills[call.fills.start + parameter] as U32
                                if fill < args.count + given
                                    . shown = "Parameter \"${name!.text}\" is given twice"
                                    . text = if fill < args.count then from-header else from-above
                                        .. from-header = "$shown, by the element's header and by this attribute; give it once"
                                        .. from-above = "$shown, by an attribute above and by this one; remove one"
                                    frame.diagnose(statement, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
                                    = false
                                if fill != args.count + given
                                    = false
                                given += 1
                                continue
                            if instances.fill-argument(call.callee, name!) == U32.max
                                = false
                            . written = panics.property-of(made, name!)
                            if written
                                panics.note-write(instance, written)
                            facts.note-element-store
                                - ElementStore(instance, id, args.count + given, place as U32, 0)
                            given += 1
                = true
= !tree.has-attributes(body)

────────────────────
+ do raise-elements
    - block SyntaxId
    - statements RowRange'SyntaxId

` Makes, where a block of markup content starts, the object of each markup element the block
` declares a name for: one written as a line of the block, or as a line of the body of such an
` element, in the order they are written, as the reference does before it runs any line of the
` block. What makes one object may read the name of an element the block has not made yet,
` which makes that one first (`raise-early`); its own is the reference's error.
. first = await-elements(statements)
if unbuilt.length == first
    =
for statement in tree.children[statements]
    raise-element(block, statement)
settle-elements(first)

────────────────────
+ do await-elements Int
    - statements RowRange'SyntaxId

` Notes, where a block starts, each markup element the block declares a name for and has not
` made, and gives how many were noted before them, for `settle-elements` where the block ends.
. first = unbuilt.length
for statement in tree.children[statements]
    await-element(statement)
= first

────────────────────
+ do settle-elements
    - first Int

` Forgets the markup elements a block noted it would make, where the block ends.
while unbuilt.length > first
    unbuilt.pop()
    awaited.pop()

────────────────────
+ do await-element
    - element SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        . slot = element-slot(element, row.id)
        if slot && !bindings.is-placed(slot)
            unbuilt += slot
            awaited += element
        do match? tree.nodes[row.body]
            | .node-block(body)
                for statement in tree.children[body.body]
                    await-element(statement)

────────────────────
+ do raise-element
    - block SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId

` Makes the object of a markup element that declares a name, then those of the lines of its
` body, under the styles and style sheets the class it names sees and the rules written in rules
` its style rules bring into view (`gather-scopes`), as the reference installs them before it
` evaluates the names a body declares. One a read made first is not made again.
do match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        . slot = element-slot(element, row.id)
        if slot && !bindings.is-placed(slot) && unbuilt.find(slot) != null
            . around = building
            building = slot
            . made = make-element(element, row)
            building = around
            assign-element(slot, made, element)
            . waited = unbuilt.find(slot)
            if waited != null
                unbuilt[waited] = no-slot
            facts.note-raised(instance, block, element)
        do match? tree.nodes[row.body]
            | .node-block(body)
                . styled = markup-styles.length
                . sheeted = markup-sheets.length
                if program.module-by-name("core/style")
                    types.clear-fault()
                    . written = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, frame.env)
                    types.clear-fault()
                    if written != invalid-type && types.intrinsic-of(written) == .class
                        do add-visible-styles(written, markup-styles, element)
                        if markup-sheets.length == 0
                            add-sheet-groups(frame.self-type, markup-sheets, sheet-levels)
                        add-sheet-groups(written, markup-sheets, sheet-levels)
                        . (start, end) = scopes-of(element)
                        if end == start && may-scope(written, row)
                            . names [Atom]
                            for name in implicit-names(written, row.type-id, row.id, tree)
                                names += program.store-atom(name)
                            . gathered [ScopeUse]
                            if !gather-scopes(written, names, row.style-rule-applications, element, written, gathered, tree)
                                decline(element)
                                =
                            record-scopes(element, gathered)
                . scoped = rule-scopes.length
                push-body-scopes(element)
                for statement in tree.children[body.body]
                    raise-element(block, statement)
                while rule-scopes.length > scoped
                    rule-scopes.pop()
                while markup-styles.length > styled
                    markup-styles.pop()
                while markup-sheets.length > sheeted
                    markup-sheets.pop()
                    sheet-levels.pop()

────────────────────
+ do names-elements Bool
    - block SyntaxId

` Whether a block whose lines are content of a markup element declares the names of the
` elements among them: the body of a `for` written as a line does, each turn.
. position = content-blocks.length
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    if content-blocks[position] == block
        = content-names[position]
= false

────────────────────
+ do check-content
    - element SyntaxId

` The function that builds what a line of a style rule generates where the rule is applied to a
` markup element, as the reference's `styleContentBuilderFunc` builds it: the element made with
` its content, as it would be anywhere, as a `MarkupElement`, under the styles, the style sheets and
` the rules written in rules its context holds, at the layer it holds, with no content generated
` by the rules the markup it makes applies (`generating`). A rule seen under the state cells of
` `when`s is seen under those it keeps (`content-cell`), and the values of the rule around one are
` kept (`content-values`), as the reference's closure captures its frames. It answers that type,
` and lets out what making the element raises. An element written with a name is declined.
prepare()
. host = types.well-known-type("core/markup", "MarkupElement")
. held = instances.contexts[instances.rows[instance].context]
. named = false
do match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        named = row.id != 0
if host == invalid-type || named
    decline(element)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
instances.set-returns(instance, host, host, .return-declared)
for position in 0 .. < held.styles
    markup-styles += instances.context-types[held.first + held.styles - 1 - position]
for position in held.first + held.styles .. < held.first + held.styles + held.sheets
    markup-sheets += instances.context-types[position]
    sheet-levels += instances.context-levels[position]
sheets-given = true
. kept U32
for position in held.scope-first .. < held.scope-first + held.scopes
    . scope = instances.context-scopes[position]
    . place = instances.context-valued[position]
    . values = if place == U32.max then U32.max else content-values(scope, place)
    . count = instances.context-cells[position]
    if count != 0
        . links = U32.max
        for depth in 0 .. < count - 1
            links = facts.scope-link(content-cell(scope, kept + depth, count - 1 - depth), links)
        rule-scopes += ScopeUse(scope, content-cell(scope, kept + count - 1, 0), values, links)
        kept += count
    else
        rule-scopes += ScopeUse(scope, U32.max, values)
scopes-given = true
layer-given = held.layer
batched += false
. made = infer(element)
batched.pop()
if made != invalid-type && made != no-type
    conversions.convert(element, element, made, host, .reason-return)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
_ do binds-property Bool
    - statement SyntaxId

` Whether a markup element gives a function of its own its name's object, as one whose body
` gives slots content does, and the name is a property of the class the markup is run on.
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-markup(row)
        = row.id != 0 && nested-decl-of(row.id) != 0 && names-property(row.id)
= false

────────────────────
_ do give-binder Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` Types the function that gives a markup element's name its object, where its body gives
` slots content, as the `MarkupIdBinder` the constructor is given after the functions that
` build the slots: before those, so that what they are given reads the name as the object.
` The name must be one the element is made in place for, or, where no block declares it, as
` under an `if` written as a line, a property the markup of the class declares for it.
. slot = element-slot(element, name)
. decl = nested-decl-of(name)
. binds = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupIdBinder", class)
. held = if slot then bindings.is-placed(slot) else names-content-property(element, name)
if !held || decl == 0 || binds == invalid-type
    decline(element)
    = false
. callee = demand-nested(decl, class)
if callee == no-instance
    decline(element)
    = false
. closure = intern-nested(decl)
facts.set-node-type(instance, name, closure)
= conversions.convert(name, name, closure, binds, .reason-markup-slot) != invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do supply-slots Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` The slots of the markup written in a class that the lines of a markup element's body give
` content, each line an element that binds a slot by name, or the one line that is no attribute
` and binds none, which gives the default slot. Each is built by a function of its own, typed
` here for the type the slot's outlet declares, and made the `MarkupSlotBuilder` of that type
` the constructor is given, after its other arguments, in the order of the slots' names, the
` default one first, as the reference orders them. A name bound twice is the reference's error,
` as is one the class declares no slot of. Content the default slot is given in another shape,
` or which a class declaring none is given by a line the module builder took for it, is
` declined. What a slot is given is made under the styles the element's own body sees, as the
` reference makes it under the element's context. Slots of a class whose slots have no shape
` here (`class-outlets`) are declined, whose outlets are checked wherever an element of it is
` written, as the reference finds them there.
` An element written with a name gives its constructor last the function that gives the name
` the object (`give-binder`). The name of each slot is pushed on the names, and the type of its
` builder on the types. Answers false where the element is not made.
. lines [SyntaxId]
if wraps-default(body)
    lines += body
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            if binds-slot(statement) || tree.holds-fills(statement)
                lines += statement
. outlets = types.intrinsic-of(class) == .class && holds-outlets(class)
if lines.length == 0 && !outlets
    = true
if types.intrinsic-of(class) != .class || types.completions[class].has-variables
    decline(element)
    = false
. names [Atom]
. wanted [TypeId]
. items [TypeId]
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
if !class-outlets(class, names, wanted, items)
    if facts.diagnostics.length == reported
        decline(element)
    = false
. defaulted = names.find(program.store-atom("")) != null
if defaulted && gives-default(body)
    decline(element)
    = false
if lines.length == 0
    = true
. name SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        name = row.id
. binder = if name != 0 then types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupIdBinder", class) else no-type
if name != 0 && !give-binder(element, name, class)
    = false
. styles [TypeId]
if program.module-by-name("core/style")
    for style in markup-styles
        styles += style
    if !add-visible-styles(class, styles, element)
        = false
. sheets [TypeId]
. levels [U32]
visible-sheets(class, sheets, levels)
. given [Atom]
. builders [TypeId]
. scopes [ScopeUse]
. scoped = slot-scopes-for(element, class, scopes)
if !give-lines(lines, names, wanted, items, styles, sheets, levels, given, builders, class, scopes, scoped, false)
    = false
for offset in 0 .. < given.length
    scratch.names.push(given[offset])
    scratch.types.push(builders[offset])
if binder != no-type
    scratch.names.push(program.store-atom(binder-slot))
    scratch.types.push(binder)
= true

────────────────────
+ do give-choices Bool
    - control SyntaxId
    - names [Atom]
    - wanted [TypeId]
    - items [TypeId]
    - styles [TypeId]
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - levels [U32]
    - given [Atom]
    - builders [TypeId]
    - class TypeId
    - scopes [ScopeUse]
    - scoped Bool
    - keeps-own Bool
    - seen [Atom]

if keeps-own
    frame.diagnose(control, .stated, program.store-atom("A subclass fills its base's slots with lines of its content, not inside an if or match"))
    = false
. filled [Atom]
. firsts [SyntaxId]
for arm in tree.region-arms(control)
    . fills [SyntaxId]
    do match? tree.nodes[tree.region-arm-body(arm)]
        | .node-block(block)
            for line in tree.children[block.body]
                if tree.fills-slot(line)
                    fills += line
    if fills.length == 0
        continue
    for line in fills
        if tree.nodes[line] is .node-markup-slot-forward
            frame.diagnose(line, .stated, program.store-atom("A slot is not passed on with <+ inside an if or match; write <+ as a line of the element's body"))
            = false
    . pattern = tree.arm-pattern(arm)
    . bound [Atom]
    if pattern != 0
        tree.pattern-names(pattern, bound)
    if pattern != 0 && tree.nodes[arm] is .node-if-block
        frame.diagnose(pattern, .stated, program.store-atom("An if that fills a slot tests a condition, not a pattern; write is or == instead"))
        = false
    if bound.length != 0
        frame.diagnose(pattern, .stated, program.store-atom("A match arm that fills a slot binds no names; test the subject without binding, as |= value or a type alone does"))
        = false
    . arm-given [Atom]
    . arm-builders [TypeId]
    . arm-mark = scratch.narrowings.mark
    . known = frame.save-members()
    narrow-arm(control, arm)
    . gave = give-lines(fills, names, wanted, items, styles, sheets, levels, arm-given, arm-builders, class, scopes, scoped, keeps-own)
    frame.pop-narrowing(arm-mark)
    frame.restore-members(known)
    if !gave
        = false
    for line in fills
        . name = tree.filled-name(line)
        if name && filled.find(name) == null
            filled += name
            firsts += line
. selector = types.well-known-type("core/markup", "MarkupSlotSelector")
. anchor = tree.selector-anchor(control)
. decl = if anchor != 0 then nested-decl-of(anchor) else 0u32
if selector == invalid-type || decl == 0 || demand-nested(decl, no-type) == no-instance
    decline(control)
    = false
. closure = intern-nested(decl)
if conversions.convert(anchor, anchor, closure, selector, .reason-markup-slot) == invalid-type
    = false
. index = types.index-type
for offset in 0 .. < filled.length
    . name = filled[offset]
    . first = firsts[offset]
    if seen.find(name) != null || given.find(name) != null
        frame.diagnose(first, .stated, program.store-atom("Duplicate slot content"))
        = false
    seen += name
    . position = names.find(name)!
    if items[position] != no-type
        frame.diagnose(first, .stated, program.store-atom("A repeated slot cannot be filled inside an if or match"))
        = false
    . content = wanted[position]
    . choice = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupSlotChoice", content)
    . builder = builder-type(content, no-type)
    if choice == invalid-type || builder == invalid-type
        decline(first)
        = false
    . markup = types.markup-host-decl.module
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    scratch.types.push(content)
    scratch.types.push(selector)
    scratch.types.push(index)
    . create = calls.demand-runtime-call(markup, no-type, program.store-atom("markup-slot-choice"), mark, 1)
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    scratch.types.push(content)
    scratch.types.push(choice)
    scratch.types.push(index)
    scratch.types.push(builder)
    . fill = calls.demand-runtime-call(markup, no-type, program.store-atom("markup-slot-arm"), mark, 1)
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if create == no-instance || fill == no-instance
        decline(first)
        = false
    facts.slot-choices += SlotChoice(instance, control, first, choice, create, fill, closure)
    add-slot(name, choice, given, builders)
= true

────────────────────
_ do narrow-arm
    - control SyntaxId
    - arm SyntaxId

for other in tree.region-arms(control)
    do match? tree.nodes[other]
        | .node-if-block(row)
            narrowing.narrow-condition(row.condition, other == arm)
    if other == arm
        =

────────────────────
+ do forwards-choice Bool
    - name Atom

. filling = filling-checker()
if !filling
    = false
. argument = instances.slot-argument(filling.instance, name)
= argument != U32.max && chosen-slot(instances.argument-type(filling.instance, argument)) != no-type

────────────────────
+ do class-outlets Bool
    - class TypeId
    - names [Atom]
    - wanted [TypeId]
    - items [TypeId]

` The slots the markup written in a class declares by its outlets, each named, the default one
` by the empty text, with the type its outlet declares, and the type of the item it gives the
` function that builds it where the slot repeats, or no type: every outlet written in the
` markup but one in the body of another, which is content the other mounts where it is given
` none, those of the classes above it first, from the top. A name declared twice, in one class
` or two, and an outlet that repeats with no type for its item, are the reference's errors,
` reported where the class is written in this module and else declined. An outlet whose type
` names nothing is reported where the type is written, in whichever module that is, since the
` element fails before the class's own markup is checked. A slot its markup
` forwards is declared as `level-slots` says. The slots of a class are looked for with it, and
` then each class above it, marked as being looked for (`outlet-classes`), as the reference marks
` them (`recursing-class`). Slots of a class whose markup passes an outlet as an argument have
` no shape here: answers false.
outlet-classes += class
. base = types.base-of(class)
. complete = if base then class-outlets(base, names, wanted, items) else true
if complete
    complete = level-slots(class, names, wanted, items)
outlet-classes.pop()
= complete

────────────────────
_ do recursing-class TypeId
    - class TypeId

` The first of a class and those above it whose slots are being looked for, from the class up,
` which the reference reports looking for again, or no type.
. level TypeId? = class
while level
    if outlet-classes.find(level) != null
        = level
    level = types.base-of(level)
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do level-slots Bool
    - class TypeId
    - names [Atom]
    - wanted [TypeId]
    - items [TypeId]

` The slots the markup written in one class declares, not counting those of the classes above
` it, added to those found so far, as `class-outlets` finds them. A line of an element's body
` that forwards a slot declares the slot of that name the element's class declares, where it
` declares one, as the reference takes it. Where that class's slots are being looked for, it
` is the reference's error, at the element, reported where the class is written in this module
` and else declined.
. ref = class-ref(types, class)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. content SyntaxId = 0
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(row)
        content = row.content
if content == 0
    = true
. found [SyntaxId]
for node in owner.tree.subtree-start(content) .. < content
    do match? owner.tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-slot-outlet(row)
            if owner.tree.argument-element(node) != 0
                = false
            found += node
        | .node-markup-slot-forward
            found += node
. forwarded [SyntaxId]
for node in found
    do match? owner.tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-markup-slot-forward(row)
            forwarded += row.outlet
. args = RowRange'TypeId()
do match? types.rows[class]
    | .type-class(row)
        args = row.args
. env = types.class-env-for(ref.module, ref.decl, args, class)
. complete = true
for outlet in found
    . inner = forwarded.find(outlet) != null
    for other in found
        do match? owner.tree.nodes[other]
            | .node-slot-outlet(row)
                if row.body != 0 && after-start && outlet <= row.body
                    inner = true
                .. after-start = owner.tree.subtree-start(row.body) <= outlet
    if inner
        continue
    do match? owner.tree.nodes[outlet]
        | .node-markup-slot-forward(row)
            . name = owner.tree.identifier-name(row.slot-binding)
            . body = owner.tree.holder-of(outlet)
            . element = owner.tree.holder-of(body)
            if !(owner.tree.nodes[element] is .node-markup)
                . control = owner.tree.arm-control(body)
                if control != 0
                    element = owner.tree.holder-of(owner.tree.holder-of(control))
            . host = no-type
            do match? owner.tree.nodes[element]
                | .node-markup(made)
                    host = types.evaluate-type(ref.module, owner.tree, made.type-id, env)
            if !name || host == invalid-type
                complete = false
                break
            if host == no-type || types.intrinsic-of(host) != .class
                continue
            . recursing = recursing-class(host)
            if recursing != no-type
                if ref.module == module
                    frame.diagnose(element, .stated, program.store-atom("Recursive markup slot signature discovery for ${type-short-name(types, recursing)}"))
                complete = false
                break
            . held [Atom]
            . contents [TypeId]
            . kept [TypeId]
            if !class-outlets(host, held, contents, kept)
                complete = false
                break
            . position = held.find(name)
            if position == null
                continue
            if names.find(name) != null
                if ref.module == module
                    frame.diagnose
                        - row.slot-binding
                        - .stated
                        - program.store-atom("Duplicate slot outlet")
                complete = false
                break
            names += name
            wanted += contents[position]
            items += kept[position]
        | .node-slot-outlet(row)
            . name = program.store-atom("")
            if row.name != 0
                name = owner.tree.identifier-name(row.name) ?? name
            if names.find(name) != null
                if ref.module == module
                    frame.diagnose(outlet, .stated, program.store-atom("Duplicate slot outlet"))
                complete = false
                break
            types.clear-fault()
            . type = types.evaluate-type(ref.module, owner.tree, row.type-id, env)
            if type == invalid-type
                . message = types.fault ?? program.store-atom("Type not found")
                types.clear-fault()
                facts.record-diagnostic(instance, ref.module, row.type-id, .stated, message)
            if type == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(type) != .class
                complete = false
                break
            . item = no-type
            do match? owner.tree.nodes[row.slot-parameter]
                | .node-markup-slot-parameter(parameter)
                    if parameter.type-id == 0
                        if ref.module == module
                            frame.diagnose
                                - parameter.name
                                - .stated
                                - program.store-atom
                                    - "Repeated slot outlet requires a slot parameter type"
                        complete = false
                        break
                    item = types.evaluate-type(ref.module, owner.tree, parameter.type-id, env)
                    if item == invalid-type
                        complete = false
                        break
            names += name
            wanted += type
            items += item
types.env-release(env)
= complete

────────────────────
+ do holds-outlets Bool
    - class TypeId

` Whether the markup a class writes, or that of a class above it, holds a slot outlet or
` forwards a slot.
. level TypeId? = class
while level
    if writes-outlets(level)
        = true
    level = types.base-of(level)
= false

────────────────────
_ do writes-outlets Bool
    - class TypeId

` Whether the markup a class writes, not counting that of the classes above it, holds a slot
` outlet or forwards a slot.
. ref = class-ref(types, class)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(row)
        if row.content != 0
            for node in owner.tree.subtree-start(row.content) .. < row.content
                if owner.tree.nodes[node] is .node-slot-outlet || slot-forward
                    = true
                .. slot-forward = owner.tree.nodes[node] is .node-markup-slot-forward
= false

────────────────────
+ do infer-outlet TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTSlotOutlet

` A slot outlet of the markup written in a class, in the function that fills an object of it,
` or in a function written in that one, which reaches what the filling function was given
` through the local that holds it (`builder-slot`). Its node is of the type it declares: the one
` the function that builds the slot gives, which the filling function was given for the slot
` by the constructor; or else, where it was given none, the one the element its body writes
` makes, cast to that type, made where the outlet is and the line of no element. Nothing is
` mounted where it has neither. Where the slot repeats, the function that builds it is given
` the item the outlet names, as the type it declares for it. The local its name declares holds
` the node. Content of several lines, or one `if`, `match` or loop of content, is built into a
` node of the slot's type made with no arguments (`wrap`), as the reference builds it. Then each
` line of its body that assigns gives the node a property as an attribute gives an element's
` object one, and one whose value read something tracked is given again by a function of its
` own, owned by the node. The style rules the outlet applies after `•`, then the lines of its
` body that declare styles, declare them for the node at a site of the outlet's own, as the
` reference's `compileSlotOverlay` does, seeing the style sheets of the markup but none of the
` node's class (`overlaying`). An outlet anywhere but the markup of a class, one whose item is
` read again where the row it is in is bound to another, body content of one line that is no
` element, and content built into a node under a batch where roots are not put off, which the
` reference puts under the batch, are declined. A type that names nothing is reported where it
` is written, as an element's is. Where it is given a builder, the locals its
` content declares are built nowhere here (`leave-unbuilt`), nor, where it mounts nothing, those
` its attributes declare. One that is a markup branch region
` (`outlet-region`) is built by the function of its one arm, which reads the item plainly and
` gives its name nothing; one of those given no builder is declined.
. filling = filling-checker()
if !filling
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
types.clear-fault()
. content = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, filling.frame.env)
if content == invalid-type
    if !report-circular() && !report-fault(row.type-id)
        frame.diagnose(row.type-id, .stated, program.store-atom("Type not found"))
    = invalid-type
if types.intrinsic-of(content) != .class
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. name = program.store-atom("")
if row.name != 0
    name = tree.identifier-name(row.name) ?? name
. item = no-type
. given SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[row.slot-parameter]
    | .node-markup-slot-parameter(parameter)
        if parameter.type-id != 0
            item = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, parameter.type-id, filling.frame.env)
        given = parameter.name
        if item == invalid-type || item == no-type
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
. lines [SyntaxId]
do match? tree.nodes[row.body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            if !(tree.nodes[statement] is .node-assign)
                lines += statement
. argument = instances.slot-argument(filling.instance, name)
. rebuilt = frame.declaration.kind == .branch-arm-decl && frame.declaration.syntax == id
if rebuilt && argument == U32.max && !tree.builds-outlet-alone(id)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. held = no-slot
. fallback SyntaxId = 0
. picks = no-type
. supplied = argument != U32.max
if supplied
    . builder = instances.argument-type(filling.instance, argument)
    . chosen = chosen-slot(builder)
    if chosen != no-type
        if frame.declaration.is-content || given != 0
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        picks = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupSlotBuilder", chosen)
        builder = picks
    if !frame.declaration.is-content
        held = builder-slot(name)
        if held == no-slot
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        argument = U32.max
    if given != 0
        . value = infer(given)
        if value == invalid-type
            = invalid-type
        if !rebuilt && (facts.plan-of(instance, given) == .plan-row-item || reads-getter(given))
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        if conversions.convert(given, given, value, item, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
            = invalid-type
    . produced = calls.builder-call(id, builder, if given == 0 then 0 else 1)
    if produced == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
    if produced != content
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    if !hold-cells(id, rule-scopes)
        = invalid-type
    if row.body != 0 && picks == no-type
        leave-unbuilt(row.body)
if supplied && picks == no-type
    fallback = 0
else if lines.length == 0
    if picks == no-type
        facts.slot-outlets += SlotOutlet(instance, id, U32.max, 0, content)
        if row.body != 0
            leave-unbuilt(row.body)
        = no-type
else if lines.length > 1 || tree.is-control-line(lines[0])
    fallback = row.body
    if in-batch() && !defers-roots()
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    . made = wrap(fallback, content)
    if made == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
    if conversions.convert(fallback, fallback, made, content, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
else
    fallback = lines[0]
    do match tree.nodes[fallback]
        | .node-markup(element)
            if element.slot-binding != 0
                decline(fallback)
                = invalid-type
        ??
            decline(fallback)
            = invalid-type
    . made = infer(fallback)
    if made == invalid-type || made == no-type
        = invalid-type
    if conversions.convert(fallback, fallback, made, content, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
facts.slot-outlets += SlotOutlet(instance, id, argument, fallback, content, held, given, no-instance, picks)
. named = declaring-slot(row.name) if row.name != 0 && !rebuilt
if named && bindings.slots[named].group == id
    frame.assign(named, content)
. outer-overlay = preparing
preparing = preparing.overlaying = true
preparing = preparing.site = 0
element-scopes.clear()
empty-shared = false
. applied = apply-written-rules(id, content, row.style-rule-applications, 0)
element-scopes.clear()
. declared = applied != U32.max && declare-styles(id, content, row.body, applied)
preparing = outer-overlay
if !declared
    = invalid-type
do match? tree.nodes[row.body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in tree.children[block.body]
            do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-assign(attribute)
                    if attribute.op == .bind-op
                        misplaced-binding(statement)
                        = invalid-type
                    if styles-attribute(attribute.op, content, style-name(tree, attribute.lhs))
                        continue
                    if attribute-type(statement, attribute.op, attribute.lhs, attribute.rhs, content) == invalid-type
                        = invalid-type
settle-attributes(row.body, content, row.type-id)
= content

────────────────────
_ do outlet-name Atom
    - row ASTSlotOutlet

. name = program.store-atom("")
if row.name != 0
    name = tree.identifier-name(row.name) ?? name
= name

────────────────────
+ do outlet-choice TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        =? no-type if row.slot-parameter != 0
        . filling = filling-checker()
        =? no-type if !filling
        . argument = instances.slot-argument(filling.instance, outlet-name(row))
        =? no-type if argument == U32.max
        = chosen-slot(instances.argument-type(filling.instance, argument))
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do check-chosen-outlet TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - parent TypeId
    - slot TypeId

do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        = check-chosen-region(id, row, parent, slot)
decline(id)
= invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do check-chosen-region TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTSlotOutlet
    - parent TypeId
    - slot TypeId

. tree-host = derived-interface(parent, types.markup-tree-host-decl)
. content = if tree-host != no-type then first-arg(tree-host) else no-type
. filling = filling-checker()
if content == no-type || content == invalid-type || !filling || in-batch()
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if !makes-region(parent)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    .. message = "Markup branch host ${type-source(types, parent)} must declare markup-make-region, or extend MarkupNode"
    = invalid-type
. name = outlet-name(row)
. argument = instances.slot-argument(filling.instance, name)
. choice = instances.argument-type(filling.instance, argument)
. held = no-slot
if !frame.declaration.is-content
    held = builder-slot(name)
    if held == no-slot
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    argument = U32.max
. alone = tree.builds-outlet-alone(id)
. builder = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupBranchBuilder", content)
. arm = if alone && builder != invalid-type then check-chosen-arm(id, row, content, builder) else no-type
if alone && (arm == no-type || arm == invalid-type)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(slot)
scratch.types.push(content)
scratch.types.push(parent)
scratch.types.push(parent)
scratch.types.push(choice)
if alone
    scratch.types.push(builder)
    scratch.types.push(types.bool-type)
. call = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.markup-host-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom(if alone then "markup-chosen-arm" else "markup-chosen-slot")
    - mark
    - 3
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if call == no-instance || !raises-out(id, call)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. fallback = if alone && tree.falls-back(row) then row.body else 0
facts.slot-outlets += SlotOutlet(instance, id, argument, fallback, slot, held, 0, call, no-type, arm)
. made = instances.signatures[call].returns
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, made)
= made

────────────────────
_ do check-chosen-arm TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTSlotOutlet
    - content TypeId
    - builder TypeId

. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id)
. decl = nested-decl-of(id)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot || decl == 0 || bindings.slots[resolution.slot - 1].syntax != id
    = no-type
frame.assign(resolution.slot - 1, types.void-type)
. named = declaring-slot(row.name) if row.name != 0
if named && bindings.slots[named].group == id
    . filling = filling-checker()
    if filling
        . made = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, filling.frame.env)
        if made != invalid-type
            frame.assign(named, made)
. outer-batch = region
region = region.batch = false
region = region.root = resolution.slot - 1
. demanded = demand-nested(decl, content)
region = outer-batch
if demanded == no-instance
    = no-type
. closure = intern-nested(decl)
if conversions.convert(id, id, closure, builder, .reason-markup-arm) == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
= closure

────────────────────
+ do check-outlet-arm TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - parent TypeId

. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id)
. decl = nested-decl-of(id)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot || decl == 0 || bindings.slots[batch].syntax != id
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. batch = resolution.slot - 1
. rooted = in-batch()
frame.assign(batch, if rooted then batch-type() else types.void-type)
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        . named = declaring-slot(row.name) if row.name != 0
        . filling = filling-checker()
        if named && filling && bindings.slots[named].group == id
            . content = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type-id, filling.frame.env)
            if content != invalid-type
                frame.assign(named, content)
. outer-batch = region
region = region.batch = rooted
region = region.root = batch
. made = demand-nested(decl, parent)
region = outer-batch
if made == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. closure = intern-nested(decl)
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, closure)
. builder = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupBranchBuilder", parent)
if builder == invalid-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if conversions.convert(id, id, closure, builder, .reason-markup-arm) == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if calls.builder-call(id, builder, 1) == invalid-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
= types.void-type

────────────────────
_ do leave-unbuilt
    - body SyntaxId

` Gives each local a body declares, which nothing here runs, the void type, so that the
` environment that holds those a nested function would capture has room for none of them: the
` content an outlet mounts where it is given none, in a function given a builder for it.
. start = tree.subtree-start(body)
. range = bindings.bindings[frame.binding].slots
for offset in 0 .. < range.count
    . slot = range.start + offset
    . syntax = bindings.slots[slot].syntax
    if syntax >= start && syntax <= body && frame.known(slot) == no-type
        frame.assign(slot, types.void-type)

────────────────────
_ do store-arguments Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId

` Keeps, for each argument of a markup element whose parameter has the name of a property of
` the element's class, that the argument is stored in the property once the object is made,
` converted as a value assigned to the property is. False where such a store has no shape
` here: an argument written with a name or a `?`, or given to a variadic parameter, a
` property that is not stored in the object or is private to another module, or an array,
` whose storage the runtime is told is replaced.
. fact = facts.latest-call(instance, id)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].callee == no-instance
    = args.count == 0
. callee = instances.rows[facts.calls[fact].callee]
. owner = program.modules[callee.module]
do match? owner.decls[callee.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        . position U32
        for arg in tree.children[args]
            if tree.nodes[arg] is .node-argument
                = false
            if position < fn.args.count
                . shape = owner.arg-pool[fn.args.start + position]
                . place = property-named(made, shape.name) if shape.name
                if place
                    . property = types.properties[place]
                    . given = facts.node-type(instance, arg)
                    if shape.is-variadic || property.storage-kind != .storage-eager
                        = false
                    if is-hidden(property, shape.name!, .setter-decl)
                        = false
                    . declared = property.type
                    if declared == no-type
                        declared = demand-member(property, made, shape.name!)
                    if declared == no-type || declared == invalid-type
                        = false
                    if is-array-value(declared)
                        = false
                    if conversions.convert(arg, arg, given, declared, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
                        = false
                    . written = panics.property-of(made, shape.name!)
                    if written
                        panics.note-write(instance, written)
                    facts.note-element-store
                        - ElementStore(instance, id, position, place as U32, arg)
            position += 1
        = true
= args.count == 0

────────────────────
+ do content-parent TypeId
    - block SyntaxId

` The type of the markup element a block's lines are content of, or no type for a block
` that is not such a one.
. position = content-blocks.length
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    if content-blocks[position] == block
        = content-parents[position]
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do outlet-region SyntaxId
    - outlet SyntaxId

` The parameter of a slot outlet that is a markup branch region of one arm, the outlet, at which
` the region is written, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[outlet]
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        = if row.slot-parameter != 0 && region-slot then row.slot-parameter else 0u32
            .. region-slot = is-region(row.slot-parameter)
= 0

────────────────────
+ do region-ensure InstanceId?
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - batched Bool
    - reason ConversionReason

` The call that puts a markup region under the batch the reference finds for its host, as
` `applyMarkupBatchRoot` does: none where no batch is found or the region is no markup host.
` The region is converted at the `if` or `for` to the host for the given reason, and the
` batch to the optional the call takes. One that has no shape here is declined, which is
` answered with nothing.
if !batched || !is-markup-host(made)
    = no-instance
. host = derived-interface(made, types.markup-host-decl)
. optional = types.optional-of(batch-type())
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(host)
scratch.types.push(optional)
. ensure = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.markup-host-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("ensure-markup-root")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if ensure == no-instance || !raises-out(id, ensure)
    decline(id)
    = null
conversions.convert(id, id, made, host, reason)
conversions.convert(id, id, batch-type(), optional, .reason-markup-root)
= ensure

────────────────────
+ do makes-region Bool
    - host TypeId

` Whether a markup host makes the regions of live loops and branches: a class declares
` `markup-make-region`, itself or in a base class, which the markup runtime calls for an empty
` region of the host's content to hold the region's controller. A host that is no class is left
` to the runtime.
=? true if types.intrinsic-of(host) != .class
= declares-method(host, program.store-atom("markup-make-region"))

────────────────────
+ do check-loop-region TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - parent TypeId

` A markup loop region, as the reference compiles one:
` one header, whose pattern is a name alone or none, with no clause but `keyed by`,
` by whose last one a function of its own keys each row (`check-key`).
` Its container is read in a live action of the region's own, where its read of a collection
` is no change the action follows, since the region observes the collection itself, and is the
` region's source as `loop-source` says. The host the `for` is content of must be a
` `MarkupElement`, whose `MarkupParent` gives the type of its content. Each row is built by a
` function of its own given the item, which gives one element as the host's content, made a
` `MarkupRowBuilder` at the `for`; that of a keyed loop over a collection is given a
` `MarkupRowItem` that holds the item, and made a `MarkupCollectionRowBuilder`. The key's
` function is made a `MarkupKeyBuilder` at its clause. A row whose body is not one element, as
` `row-region` says, is built as an arm is, into a region of its own: its function is given the
` region after the item, made a `MarkupRegionRowBuilder` at the `for`, and the markup runtime's
` `markup-region-row`, or `markup-region-keyed-row`, makes the builder of it, which makes the
` region of the host for each row. The markup runtime makes the region of
` the host, the builders and the source, given last, as `loop-source` says, keyed where the loop
` is, and gives the region a source again by a replacer of its own; the region is the line's
` value, which the host takes. The host and the region are kept, in the
` two locals no name reaches declared at the `for`, for the function that reads the container
` again, which the action runs: made by
` `make-owner-markup-action`, owned by the region and marked structural. Where a batch is found
` for the host, the host itself where it is a batch and else the one in force, the region is
` put under it by `ensure-markup-root` once made; where one is in force it is kept in a third
` local no name reaches, which the rows are built under, and the action is made with it by
` `make-markup-action`. One whose region is no class is declined; one of a class with events
` is kept as any other, as the reference keeps it. One whose content is a class and whose host
` makes no regions, as `makes-region` says, is an error at the `for`.
. loop SyntaxId = 0
. body SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        loop = row.loop
        body = row.body
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
. container SyntaxId = 0
. clause SyntaxId = 0
. chained SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        pattern = row.pattern
        container = row.container
        clause = row.clause
        chained = row.next
if chained != 0
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Combined markup loops not supported"))
    = invalid-type
if pattern != 0 && !(tree.nodes[pattern] is .node-type-capture)
    frame.diagnose
        - pattern
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Markup loop patterns must be simple captures")
    = invalid-type
. current = clause
. filters = 0
while current != 0
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    do match? tree.nodes[current]
        | .node-clause(row)
            if row.op == .when-clause
                filters += 1
            if row.op != .keyed-by-clause && row.op != .when-clause
                frame.diagnose
                    - current
                    - .stated
                    - program.store-atom("A markup loop that follows state takes only keyed by and when clauses")
                = invalid-type
            if filters > 1
                frame.diagnose
                    - current
                    - .stated
                    - program.store-atom("A markup loop that follows state takes one when clause; join its conditions with &&")
                = invalid-type
            next = row.next
    current = next
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. keyed = tree.keyed-clause(loop)
. read = infer(container, Want().adding(.want-observed))
if read == invalid-type || read == no-type
    = invalid-type
. found = loop-source(id, container, read)
. item = found.item
. source = found.given
if item == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if !is-markup-host(parent)
    frame.diagnose
        - id
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Dynamic markup loop parent must implement MarkupElement")
    = invalid-type
. tree-host = derived-interface(parent, types.markup-tree-host-decl)
. content = if tree-host != no-type then first-arg(tree-host) else no-type
if content == no-type || content == invalid-type || types.completions[content].has-variables
    frame.diagnose
        - id
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Dynamic markup loop host content type could not be resolved")
    = invalid-type
if types.intrinsic-of(content) == .class && !makes-region(parent)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    .. message = "Markup loop host ${type-source(types, parent)} must declare markup-make-region, or extend MarkupNode"
    = invalid-type
. regioned = tree.row-region(body)
if !knows-getters(body)
    = invalid-type
. refreshes = keyed != 0 && found.kind == "collection"
. given = if refreshes then types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupRowItem", item) else item
. builder = types.well-known-type-of
    - "core/markup"
    - if refreshes then "MarkupCollectionRowBuilder" else "MarkupRowBuilder"
    - item
    - content
. shaped = if regioned then types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupRegionRowBuilder", given, content) else builder
. decl = nested-decl-of(body)
if classless || builder == invalid-type || shaped == invalid-type || given == invalid-type || decl == 0
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. classless = types.intrinsic-of(content) != .class
. rooted = in-batch()
. hosted = is-batch(parent)
. outer-content = region
region = region.content = content
region = region.batch = rooted
region = region.root = resolution.slot + 2
. built = demand-nested(decl, given, if regioned then content else no-type)
region = outer-content
if built == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. closure = intern-nested(decl)
facts.set-node-type(instance, body, closure)
if conversions.convert(id, id, closure, shaped, .reason-markup-row) == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
. keyer = no-type
if keyed != 0
    keyer = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupKeyBuilder", item)
    . key = nested-decl-of(keyed)
    if keyer == invalid-type || key == 0 || demand-nested(key, item) == no-instance
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    . keying = intern-nested(key)
    facts.set-node-type(instance, keyed, keying)
    if conversions.convert(keyed, keyed, keying, keyer, .reason-markup-key) == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
. filter = tree.when-clause(loop)
. tester = no-type
if filter != 0
    tester = types.well-known-type-of("core/markup", "MarkupRowFilter", given)
    . test = nested-decl-of(filter)
    if tester == invalid-type || test == 0 || demand-nested(test, given) == no-instance
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    . testing = intern-nested(test)
    facts.set-node-type(instance, filter, testing)
    if conversions.convert(filter, filter, testing, tester, .reason-markup-key) == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
demand-live-runtime()
. live = instances.live
. markup = types.markup-host-decl.module
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. optional = types.intrinsic-of(source) == .optional
. held = if optional then types.optional-inner(source) else source
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(content)
scratch.types.push(parent)
scratch.types.push(held)
scratch.types.push(parent)
scratch.types.push(builder)
if keyer != no-type
    scratch.types.push(keyer)
scratch.types.push(source)
. creates = "markup-create-${if optional then "optional-" else ""}${if keyed != 0 then "keyed-" else ""}${found.kind}-region"
. create = calls.demand-runtime-call(markup, no-type, program.store-atom(creates), mark, 4)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
. made = if create != no-instance then instances.signatures[create].returns else no-type
if made == no-type || types.intrinsic-of(made) != .class || !is-markup-host(made) || live.has-actions == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(made)
scratch.types.push(held)
scratch.types.push(made)
scratch.types.push(source)
. replaces = "markup-replace-${if optional then "optional-" else ""}${found.kind}-source"
. replace = calls.demand-runtime-call(markup, no-type, program.store-atom(replaces), mark, 3)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if replace == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. adapts = no-instance
if regioned
    scratch.types.push(item)
    scratch.types.push(content)
    scratch.types.push(parent)
    scratch.types.push(parent)
    scratch.types.push(shaped)
    if tester != no-type
        scratch.types.push(tester)
    . kind = if tester != no-type then "filtered-row" else "row"
    . adapter = if refreshes then "markup-region-keyed-$kind" else "markup-region-$kind"
    adapts = calls.demand-runtime-call(markup, no-type, program.store-atom(adapter), mark, 3)
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if adapts == no-instance || instances.signatures[adapts].returns != builder || !raises-out(id, adapts)
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
. host = derived-interface(made, types.markup-host-decl)
scratch.types.push
    - if live.trackers != no-instance then instances.signatures[live.trackers].returns else no-type
scratch.types.push(live.callback)
scratch.types.push(if rooted then batch-type() else host)
. action = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - markup
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom(if rooted then "make-markup-action" else "make-owner-markup-action")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
. structural = mark-structural(id, made)
if action == no-instance || structural == no-instance || other-return
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. other-return = instances.signatures[action].returns != types.live-action-type
if !raises-out(id, create) || !raises-out(id, action) || !raises-out(id, structural)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if hosted
    conversions.convert(id, id, parent, batch-type(), .reason-markup-batch)
. ensure = region-ensure(id, made, rooted || hosted, .reason-markup-region)
if !ensure
    = invalid-type
conversions.convert(id, id, made, host, .reason-markup-host)
frame.assign(resolution.slot, parent)
frame.assign(resolution.slot + 1, made)
frame.assign(resolution.slot + 2, if rooted then batch-type() else types.void-type)
. outer-source = region
region = region.source = source
region = region.replace = replace
. updater = demand-lambda(intern-nested(nested-decl-of(id)), scratch.no-types)
region = outer-source
if updater == no-instance || (updater-raises && live.callback-result == no-type)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. updater-raises = instances.signatures[updater].errors.count != 0
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
facts.loop-regions += LoopRegion
    - instance
    - id
    - parent
    - content
    - source
    - create
    - updater
    - action
    - structural
    - ensure
    - hosted
    - rooted
    - replace
    - adapts
= made

────────────────────
_ do knows-getters Bool
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether the lazy declarations of the body of a markup loop region's row are those the binder
` found a getter in. One it found none in has no shape here.
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(block)
        for line in tree.children[block.body]
            do match? tree.nodes[line]
                | .node-declare(declared)
                    if declared.is-lazy && !declares-getter(declared.left)
                        decline(line)
                        = false
= true

────────────────────
+ do check-selector
    - anchor SyntaxId

. id = tree.selector-control(anchor)
prepare()
demand-live-runtime()
. selected = types.optional-of(types.index-type)
instances.set-returns(instance, selected, selected, .return-declared)
content-blocks += 0
content-parents += no-type
content-names += false
read-arms(id)
content-blocks.pop()
content-parents.pop()
content-names.pop()
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
+ do host-content
    - statement SyntaxId
    - parent TypeId

` An `if`, a `for`, and a loop written with `in` that is no function of its own, written as
` lines of a markup element's body, run their bodies as content of the same element: each body
` is noted as such while the statement is typed. A loop on a stream subscribes, and its body
` is no content, the arms of a markup branch region are content of the region, which functions
` of their own build, and the body of a markup loop region builds a row.
if is-region(statement) || is-loop-region(statement)
    =
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-if-block
        . branch = statement
        while branch != 0
            . next SyntaxId = 0
            do match? tree.nodes[branch]
                | .node-if-block(row)
                    content-blocks += tree.arm-body(branch)
                    content-parents += parent
                    content-names += false
                    next = row.next
            branch = next
    | .node-for-block(row)
        if tree.is-subscriber-loop(row.loop)
            =
        content-blocks += row.body
        content-parents += parent
        content-names += true
    | .node-iterator-expression(row)
        if nested-decl-of(statement) != 0
            =
        content-blocks += row.body
        content-parents += parent
        content-names += true

────────────────────
+ do link-content
    - statement SyntaxId
    - produced TypeId
    - parent TypeId

` A line of a markup element's body that gives a value is taken by the element: by its
` `+=`, or else its `++=`, with the value converted as an argument of the one found, or where
` the element is a markup host as `link-hosted` says. The call is kept for the line. An
` assignment, a print and a state machine give the element nothing, and a loop written as an
` expression has no shape as a line. An element no local is declared for, named for the property
` its class's markup declares for it, gives the property what the call answers, or the object
` where it answers nothing.
if untyped || produced == types.void-type || tree.is-quasi-syntax(statement)
    =
.. untyped = produced == no-type || produced == invalid-type
if tree.nodes[statement] is .node-state-machine
    =
if tree.nodes[statement] is .node-iterator-expression
    decline(statement)
    =
if is-markup-host(parent)
    link-hosted(statement, produced, parent)
    =
. content = calls.content-call(parent, program.store-atom("+="), statement, produced)
if content.taken == no-type
    content = calls.content-call(parent, program.store-atom("++="), statement, produced)
. taken = content.taken
. link = content.fact
. answered = content.answer
if taken == no-type || link == no-fact
    frame.diagnose(statement, .stated, program.store-atom("Content not accepted"))
    =
conversions.convert(statement, statement, produced, taken, .reason-argument)
. answers = no-type
. named = named-element(statement)
if named && answered != no-type
    if answered == invalid-type
        decline(statement)
        =
    if conversions.convert(statement, statement, answered, frame.slot-type(named), .reason-assignment, true, true) == invalid-type
        =
    answers = answered
facts.note-content-link(ContentLink(instance, statement, parent, taken, link, answers))
if named
    note-named(statement, if answers != no-type then answers else frame.slot-type(named))
else if content-named(statement)
    note-named
        - statement
        - if answered != no-type && answered != types.void-type then answered else produced

────────────────────
_ do link-hosted
    - statement SyntaxId
    - produced TypeId
    - parent TypeId

` A line of the body of a markup element whose class is a markup host is taken through the
` markup protocol: by the host's `markup-absorb` where the value is an argument of one, which
` keeps it in the host's own state; else by its `markup-content`, which answers the node the
` value becomes, and that node is linked as the host's last child by the markup runtime's
` `markup-append`. A line that is an element a name is declared for gives the name the node,
` converted as a value assigned to the name, which casts it, checked, to the element's class;
` but where the element gives slots content and its name is a property of the class the markup
` is run on, the name and the property keep the object, as the reference keeps it there. One no
` local is declared for, named for the property its class's markup declares for it, gives the
` property the node, or the object where the host absorbs it.
. absorbing = calls.content-call(parent, program.store-atom("markup-absorb"), statement, produced)
. absorbed = absorbing.taken
if absorbed != no-type
    conversions.convert(statement, statement, produced, absorbed, .reason-argument)
    facts.note-content-link(ContentLink(instance, statement, parent, absorbed, absorbing.fact))
    . kept = named-element(statement)
    if kept
        note-named(statement, frame.slot-type(kept))
    else if content-named(statement)
        note-named(statement, produced)
    =
. content = calls.content-call(parent, program.store-atom("markup-content"), statement, produced)
. taken = content.taken
. link = content.fact
. answered = content.answer
if taken == no-type || link == no-fact || answered == no-type
    frame.diagnose(statement, .stated, program.store-atom("Content not accepted"))
    =
. named = named-element(statement)
if answered == invalid-type
    decline(statement)
    =
conversions.convert(statement, statement, produced, taken, .reason-argument)
. kept = named && !binds-property(statement)
if kept && conversions.convert(statement, statement, answered, frame.slot-type(named!), .reason-assignment, true, true) == invalid-type
    =
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(parent)
scratch.types.push(answered)
. append = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.markup-host-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("markup-append")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if append == no-instance
    decline(statement)
    =
. answers = if kept then answered else no-type
facts.note-content-link(ContentLink(instance, statement, parent, taken, link, answers, append))
if kept
    note-named(statement, answered)
else if content-named(statement)
    note-named(statement, answered)
else if named
    note-named(statement, frame.slot-type(named))

────────────────────
_ do content-named Bool
    - statement SyntaxId

` Whether a line of content is a markup element that no block declares a local for, whose name
` is that of the property the markup of the class declares for it (`names-content-property`).
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-markup(row)
        = unslotted && names-content-property(statement, row.id)
            .. unslotted = row.id != 0 && !element-slot(statement, row.id)
= false

────────────────────
_ do names-content-property Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId

` Whether the name of a markup element is that of a property the markup of the class of the
` object the function runs on declares for its elements of that name, where the element is one
` of them: written in that markup outside any function or loop of it. The reference gives such
` a property each such element's object, as `named-place` says.
if bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, name).kind != .resolve-member
    = false
. self = frame.self-type
if self == no-type || self == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(self) != .class || lacks-self()
    = false
. text = tree.identifier-name(name)
. place = property-named(self, text) if text
if !place
    = false
. ref = declaring-decl(types, types.properties[place])
. member = owner-property(program, ref.module, ref.decl, text!)
if member == 0
    = false
. content SyntaxId = 0
do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        content = class.content
do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[member]
    | .decl-property(declared)
        = owned && tree.subtree-start(content) <= element && !enclosed
            .. owned = declared.element != 0 && ref.module == module && content > element
            .. enclosed = tree.enclosed-element(element, content)
= false

────────────────────
+ do named-element SlotId?
    - statement SyntaxId

` The local a line of content that is a markup element declares for the element, where a
` block declares one.
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-markup(row)
        = element-slot(statement, row.id)
= null

────────────────────
+ element-slot SlotId?
    - element SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId

` The local a block declares for a markup element written with a name. A name no block
` declares for the element may find a local something else declared, which is not one.
|? name == 0
    null
|? slot && bindings.slots[slot].group == element
    slot
??
    null

.. slot = declaring-slot(name)

────────────────────
+ places-across Bool
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a local a function this one is written in declares for a markup element's name is
` reached through functions that build slots alone, from this one out to the one that
` declares it.
|? !outer || !frame.is-captured(slot)
    true
|? frame.declaration.kind != .slot-decl
    false
??
    outer.places-across(slot)

────────────────────
+ do check-region
    - id SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A `do without gc` block written where code is outside the zone the collector never sees, as the
` reference outlines it: a function of its own, typed once, which reaches the locals and
` arguments of the function around it where they are kept and is called where the block is.
` What the flow knows of those locals holds in the body as in a plain block, and what the body
` leaves them as holds after it (`leave-region`). The call ends what is known of properties, as
` any call does. A block whose last line returns or raises is the reference's error. One that
` lets an error out has no shape here. A body that captures a local is given an object the
` collector owns where it runs.
if tree.ends-returning(body)
    frame.diagnose
        - id
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("GC-free do blocks cannot return from their enclosing function")
    =
. row = bindings.bindings[frame.binding]
for offset in 0 .. < row.nested.count
    . nested = bindings.nested[row.nested.start + offset]
    if nested.syntax == id
        . mask = callee-effects(frame, module, nested.decl)
        . none = scratch.no-types
        . callee = instances.intern(module, nested.decl, no-type, mask, instance, none, none, false)
        . left [Narrowed]
        if instances.rows[callee].state == .instance-unstarted
            facts.region-bodies += callee
            left = run-within(callee, this)
        if instances.signatures[callee].errors.count != 0
            decline(id)
            =
        if nested.captures.count != 0
            frame.check-allocates(id)
        facts.record-call(instance, id, callee, .call-function, scratch.no-fills, false)
        if instances.rows[callee].may-panic
            instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
        forget-assigned(nested)
        frame.keep-assigned(left)
        frame.forget-members()
        =
decline(id)

────────────────────
_ do forget-assigned
    - nested NestedFunction

` Each local a `do without gc` block assigns is known past the block as its own type, until what
` the body left it as is known again (`leave-region`): a body typed before is not typed again.
for index in 0 .. < nested.captures.count
    . capture = bindings.captures[nested.captures.start + index]
    if (capture.flags /and/ CaptureFlag.capture-assigned) == 0
        continue
    . held = slot-known(capture.slot)
    if held == no-type || held == invalid-type
        continue
    frame.push-assigned(slot-key(capture.slot), held)
    frame.reset-paths(slot-key(capture.slot))

────────────────────
+ do read-later-element TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - slot SlotId

if starts-task(slot)
    . message = "Named markup element \"${name.text}\" is read in a task started before its markup constructs it, and a task keeps what it reads as it starts; start the task after the markup"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
. class = foresee-element(slot)
if class == invalid-type || class == no-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if types.completions[class].has-variables
    . written = class-name-of(class-ref(types, class))
    . message = "Named markup element \"${name.text}\" is read in a closure made before its markup constructs it, so it needs its type arguments written after \"$written\""
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-guarded-read)
= class

────────────────────
_ do keep-element Bool
    - element SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` The local no name reaches that keeps the object of a markup element, where a function written
` in its body reads its members by name alone or one gives its arguments again, holds one of the
` element's class: the class written, as the functions that build regions of its body are typed
` with the body, and then that of the object made, which must be the same. False where it is not.
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, element)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    = true
. held = frame.slot-type(resolution.slot)
if held != no-type && held != made
    = false
frame.assign(resolution.slot, made)
= true

────────────────────
+ do writes-markup Bool

` Whether the body of the function being typed writes a markup element.
. body = frame.declaration.body
if body == 0
    = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. body
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-markup
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ is-markup-query Bool
    - type TypeId

match types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        types.ancestor-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl) || descendant-query

        .. descendant-query = types.descendants-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
    ??
        false

────────────────────
+ do content-property-type TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - line SyntaxId

` The type of the property a line of a class's markup declares (`content-property`): that of the
` value the line gives it, as each function that fills an object with the markup typed it, which
` must agree, as the reference gives the property the type of the first value stored. Where none
` has typed the line yet, a filler or constructor of the class still waiting in the queue is typed
` first, one at a time, until one has (`pending-filler`). None where none is left.
. owner-module = program.modules[ref.module]
. filler DeclId = 0
do match? owner-module.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        filler = class.content-function
. value SyntaxId = 0
do match? owner-module.tree.nodes[line]
    | .node-property-syntax(row)
        value = row.value
if filler == 0 || value == 0
    = invalid-type
while true
    . found = no-type
    for unit in 0u32 .. < (instances.rows.length as U32)
        . row = instances.rows[unit]
        if row.module == ref.module && row.decl == filler
            . typed = facts.node-type(unit, value)
            if typed != no-type && typed != invalid-type
                if found != no-type && found != typed
                    = invalid-type
                found = typed
    if found != no-type
        = found
    . pending = pending-filler(ref, filler)
    if pending == no-instance
        = invalid-type
    demand-body(pending)

────────────────────
+ do infer-content-property TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId
    - want Want

` A line of a class's markup that declares a property it gives its value (`content-property`), as
` the reference's content runs it: the value is stored in the property of the object being filled
` where the line runs, as an assignment to the property named alone stores it, and runs again
` where it reads something tracked, as a live assignment does. The line gives no content. One
` whose name its class or a class above declares too is reported (`report-content-clash`).
. left = tree.content-property-name(id)
. name = tree.identifier-name(left) if left != 0
if !name || bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, left).kind != .resolve-member
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if !owns-content-property(frame.self-type, name, id)
    report-content-clash(frame.self-type, name, id)
    = invalid-type
. assigned = infer-assign(id, .eq-op, left, value, want)
if assigned != invalid-type && facts.live-statements.length != 0
    settle-live-statement(id, left, value, facts.node-type(instance, value))
= assigned

────────────────────
_ do report-content-clash
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - id SyntaxId

` Reports the property of a name that the class whose markup holds the line `id`, or a class
` above it, declares otherwise than the line does (`content-property`), as the reference reports
` a property stored two ways: `Inherited properties must have same assignment type` at that
` declaration, where it is a stored one of this module. Any other clash, one a class below
` declares among them, is declined.
. level TypeId? = receiver
. reached = false
while level
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    reached = reached || holds-line(ref, id)
    . member = owner-property(program, ref.module, ref.decl, name)
    if member != 0
        do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[member]
            | .decl-property(row)
                if row.line != id && reached
                    if ref.module == module && !row.is-lazy
                        frame.diagnose
                            - row.syntax
                            - .stated
                            - program.store-atom
                                - "Inherited properties must have same assignment type"
                        =
                    decline(id)
                    =
    level = types.base-of(level)
decline(id)

────────────────────
_ do holds-line Bool
    - ref DeclRef
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a line of this module is one of the markup the class `ref` writes.
if ref.module != module
    = false
do match? program.modules[module].decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        = class.content != 0 && tree.subtree-start(class.content) <= id && id <= class.content
= false

────────────────────
_ do owns-content-property Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - line SyntaxId

` Whether the property of a name an object of `receiver` has is the one a line of the markup of
` its class, or of a class above, declares (`content-property`), and no class above that one
` declares one of the name.
. level TypeId? = receiver
while level
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . member = owner-property(program, ref.module, ref.decl, name)
    if member != 0
        do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[member]
            | .decl-property(row)
                if row.line != line || ref.module != module
                    = false
                . above = types.base-of(level)
                = !above || !property-named(above, name)
        = false
    level = types.base-of(level)
= false
